.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/pr-body.md:1:Part of #1757 and #1796. The branch contains the prerequisite work from #1793, #1798, #1799, #1800 and #1801, plus the corpus repairs from #1804. These dependencies need individual acceptance and sequential ghprsq integration.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/pr-body.md:5:The current review repair preserves clause exactness and ordinary distinct guards through lowering and specialization. Restricted blocking reads exact native premises separately from the coarser vocabulary quotient, so it cannot fabricate an inverse by identifying ordinary data URIs. Relaxed clauses, lossy pair bridges and unknown-count witness summaries cannot supply guaranteed blocking evidence. Valid mixed operator spellings remain certifiable. anyURI facets and enumeration equality use PurRDF's XML whitespace normalizer; finite-write bounds saturate. The native artifact fixture repair from #1782 retains real execution evidence and checks missing/mismatched receipts. Unused csv/flate2 dependencies and the reported lint defects are removed.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/pr-body.md:18:The remaining class-model work follows #1803's ownership agreement: PurRDF owns generic DL/chase engines; GMEOW owns logic semantics and world-scoped provenance. The historical released-3.0.0 benchmark does not decide the two large worlds within its selected budget. The three datatype/property-chain boundary issues are now merged upstream, beyond the latest published 3.0.1 release; current GMEOW locks still select 3.0.0. GMEOW's rule-reification defect #1805 is in active implementation on an isolated branch. Capability, production and full-gate work remain acceptance requirements.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/pr-body.md:20:Current CodeRabbit findings require reassessment against the new head. No independent completion audit or merge readiness is claimed. Principles 4, 7, 12, 15, 17, 18 and 19.
