.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1748-current.json:18:      "body": "Implementation progress under the approved plan (Principles 4, 7, 9, 17\u201319): integrated the prover branch's structural typing repairs into the shared native frontend readers. Canonical logic rules, formulas, contracts, constraints, reasoning programs, restrictions and correspondence records accept the two admitted structural declaration forms without globally equating `logic:instanceOf` with `rdf:type`. Dual typing does not duplicate extracted rules or promote structural records into domain axioms; external RDF/OWL grammar remains predicate-exact. All 18 constraint sugars reject malformed native-typed declarations.\n\nThe `math:memberCondition` formula remains owned by its set instead of becoming an unconditional global assertion. Its required owner-aware evaluation is now visible through an attributed `OWNER_SCOPED_MEMBER_CONDITION` diagnostic. This does not implement set denotation or authorize a whole-corpus consistency verdict; that diagnostic must participate in this issue's loss/coverage admission work.\n\nVerification: the native compiler and obligation selection passed all 804 tests, including five new frontend regressions; repository lint passed. No corpus production or upstream conformance testing occurred. Shared canonical coverage, pure-logic clash/distinctness consequences, result identity/admission and full gate evidence remain required implementation. The external prover branch and its commits are preserved.\n",
