.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1748-current.json:33:      "body": "Native frontend integration progress in the preserved C1 worktree:\n\n- Adopted merged PurRDF `canonical_relabel` directly, removing the compiler's canonical N-Quads serialization/reparse and preserving the native statement layer.\n- Rules now reject missing/ambiguous head or atom fields, malformed conjuncts/guards/aggregation and non-IRI predicates as attributed whole-rule errors. They no longer become weaker executable rules when an antecedent is skipped. Triple-valued fields unsupported by the current Horn record produce diagnostics instead of panics.\n- Rule declaration/scope metadata has one semantic home in the typed rule. This removes duplicate headless declarations from Common Logic round trips while retaining provenance on the executable rules.\n- Regenerated the committed CLIF ingestion fixture with an explicit O3/fat-LTO maintainer producer, outside the test runner. Reviewed diff removes only four duplicate metadata statements; actual ancestor rules and their provenance remain unchanged.\n\nVerification: 846/846 GMEOW-owned compiler and selected native integration tests passed, including both previously exposed CLIF failures; workspace development Clippy with -D warnings and make lint passed. No PurRDF conformance tests ran, and no tests produced corpus. This is focused verification, not a full gate or completion of this issue.\n\nThe complete selected-source/origin/owner inventory, admitted context-preserving execution and joint producer closure, source-to-IR mappings and authenticated coverage/run receipts remain required as specified in the body. These frontend repairs and shared preparation remain preserved implementation progress. Principles 4, 7, 9, 17\u201319.\n",
