.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1748-current.json:63:      "body": "The native source-catalog implementation will use an explicit producer boundary while preserving the current authenticated fixture cache.\n\n1. Add `stage-parse-sources` as a deterministic, recomputed producer node. It owns the original per-document native parses, exact portable document receipts, source roles/bases/spans, and one native composite/materialized base. Its ordinary carrier contains a small generated receipt graph; original RDF stays in its ephemeral typed handle.\n2. Keep `stage-source-load` persistent and selected in the existing authenticated fixture manifest. It consumes the native catalog and publishes its existing bounded graph/artifact/span contribution. Its `sourceOrigin` capability remains exclusive. The only direct real-corpus source-load test consumes its published provenance graph, so it needs no native catalog or new fixture exception.\n3. Compile-logic declares both parse-stage and source-load dependencies. It reads its selected canonical source directly from the original parsed document, retaining existing explicit import/example roles. The catalog remains an inventory, not blanket permission to assert every catalog fact.\n4. Bind complete typed handle payloads into both whole-product and selected-entity action keys, identically for live products and authenticated receipts. Memoize those small commitments at publication. Preserve published identity across span/carrier release; remove the separate span-trim digest witness and its warm hydration/write path.\n5. Release original catalog datasets after their last declared consumer through normal carrier lifetime management. Only compact required source/unit metadata may enter the persisted compiled envelope. The parse stage is a nonpersistent ancestor in `closure_receipts`, never a test-selected fixture.\n6. Carry the exact native identity chain through PurRDF's merged canonical mapping API: original source ID, composite view ID, exact typed materialized lookup, actual relabel mapping. Persist authenticated source occurrences and bindings; raw TermIds and independently guessed canonical labels are not durable identities. Symmetric blank structures require explicit attribution tests.\n\nNext compiler work remains within this issue: candidate/ownership inventory before filtering, shared formula success/error reconstruction, complete source-to-IR routing/dedup bindings, and context-aware consumer admission. No bounded corpus result or inventory count constitutes a rewrite certificate. Full calculus completion remains required under #1704/#1741.\n\nPrinciples 4, 7, 17 and 19 apply throughout. No test rebuilds the corpus; no upstream conformance suite is copied. Both cold CI generations and optimized producer checks remain required.\n",
