.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1748-current.json:78:      "body": "The merged PurRDF prerequisites are now integrated at `6aea923518e1d81a3192d77e47fc103fd003f391`. The current uncommitted implementation separates native source preparation from source publication:\n\n```\nparse-sources (original documents + one shared aggregate; recomputed, ephemeral)\n  \u251c\u2500\u2500 source-load (source-origin publication, provenance and carrier partitions)\n  \u2514\u2500\u2500 compile-logic (original native selections and retained canonical term maps)\n```\n\nThis refines the earlier proposed compiler dependency on both parse and source-load. Auditing actual reads found no required carrier output: retaining the source-load dependency would serialize two independent consumers and reintroduce a projected source boundary. Both consumers are mandatory and source-load retains its exclusive SourceOrigin capability and all publication/gate duties. The Rust plan and canonical pipeline slice now declare the same sibling dependency structure. This is required implementation within the existing scope, not a new follow-up.\n\nCatalog identity binds exact source bytes, portable document names, roles and admitted bases. The catalog itself cannot be persisted; downstream complete typed programs retain their own authenticated cache boundary. Original document handles map through the actual composite and materialized selection before applying the exact PurRDF canonical mapping. No local TermId is persisted or joined by a guessed canonical blank label. Whole-source semantic-unit inventory and source-to-IR bindings through lowering are still being implemented; this preparatory catalog does not claim complete coverage or execution certification.\n\nSeparately, native reasoning-summary publication and verification now avoid an RDF serialization/parse round trip. The last completed focused checks passed 61 native result/cache/identity tests, then 10 production Reason/Verify tests, with workspace Clippy and hygiene. The newer source-catalog patch is in focused verification and has no full-gate receipt yet.\n\nConversion removal, fusion, incremental reuse and scheduling still require separate observations on the O3/full-LTO producer. Both independent cold CI generations, all logical contracts, provenance and loss checks remain mandatory. Principles 4, 7, 9, 17\u201319.\n",
