.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1748-current.json:93:      "body": "The merged PurRDF native source integration now passes focused validation in the correspondence worktree. Nine tests passed, covering original document identity and symmetric blank anchors through composite materialization/canonical relabeling, exact byte/role/path commitments, persistent-cache refusal of the ephemeral catalog, diagnostic meta-rule behavior, and Rust/RDF DAG binding. Workspace Clippy and hygiene passed. These tests construct only small synthetic inputs or read their declared source fixtures; no corpus producer or upstream conformance suite was invoked.\n\nThe obsolete `graph/logic-compile-inputs` projection is removed from construction, helpers, constants and both attach declarations. An independent read-only audit found no remaining consumer. Source publication retains its authored/import/example partitions and all existing gates. Compilation borrows the actual native catalog alongside source-load and shares its prepared canonical source with diagnostic meta-rules, eliminating their extra canonicalization and simple query-engine lookups.\n\nFull source-unit accounting, source-to-IR bindings, selected-context native execution, complete calculus adoption and the optimized producer/full gate remain required current scope. These passing focused tests do not authorize unrestricted correspondence rewrites or close this issue. Principles 4, 7, 9, 17\u201319.\n",
