.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1748-current.json:108:      "body": "Implementation progress under #1704 in the C1 worktree (Principles 4, 7, 9, 17\u201319):\n\n- Formula validation, constraints, reasoning-program clauses/query/probes and correspondence recovery transforms now share one dataset-bound reconstruction session. Native source IDs and modal world/depth key the bounded memo (8 MiB retained payload, 4096 entries); eviction only recomputes.\n- Removed the formula extractor's second collection of all intermediate trees. Source references and recursion guards distinguish equal blank labels in different scopes.\n- Fixed modal capture of authored world-variable names and included modal bodies in occurrence-scoped sort collection. Typed failure reuse preserves source focus without transplanting path-sensitive cycle diagnostics into other recursive walks.\n- Updated the compiler implementation identity and pipeline documentation. Existing owned IR boundaries remain; this is not a claim that all intermediate materialization or lowering is eliminated.\n\nValidation: 208/208 selected compiler/correspondence tests passed, including seven new reuse/semantic regressions; repository lint passed; workspace Clippy passed with -D warnings. The synthetic selection performed no corpus generation and ran no PurRDF suite. No full gate, producer measurement, commit or merge is claimed. Existing Cargo manifest/future-compatibility findings remain tracked acceptance work.\n\nThe next boundary is still the complete semantic-unit/source-to-IR inventory and source-aware admission required here, followed by joint native selected execution and certified correspondence integration. Memo hits do not certify coverage or authorize rewrites. The remaining overlap audit, O3/full-LTO producer measurements, both independent cold CI generations and full review/merge requirements remain current scope.\n",
