.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1748-current.json:123:      "body": "Further implementation under #1704 in the C1 worktree (Principles 4, 7, 9, 17\u201319):\n\n- Added the shared structural source graph before extraction/lowering. It retains declared versus required unit families and separates ownership, component, backing, graph/module/standpoint, import and provenance relationships.\n- Prepared source selections now retain original per-document byte/base/role receipts and native original-to-canonical node occurrences. Two documents contributing one named law keep both origins; equal anonymous labels remain distinct. No reparsing or label-guessing join is used.\n- Fixed undeclared recovery owners hiding orphan cases, invalid owner/target handling, and source focus lost during failed Horn lowering. Mathematical backing and owner-scoped membership remain distinct.\n- Included native RDF 1.2 reifiers, annotations and quoted-statement graph placement in the inventory and origin mapping. Physical source positions remain distinct while duplicate representations of one invalid use yield one diagnostic.\n\nValidation: final 223/223 selected compiler/correspondence/source-catalog tests passed; repository lint and workspace Clippy with -D warnings passed. No corpus producer, full gate, PurRDF suite, commit or merge was run. Producer profile contracts are unchanged. Existing Cargo manifest/future-compatibility findings remain current acceptance work.\n\nThis remains a structural inventory, not a completed CompiledTheory or persistent source-to-IR/execution certificate. The next required boundary here is the frontend's native RDF 1.2 accessor path: ordinary quad-only readers still need to consume native statement-layer scope without conversion/materialization. Then finish all unit/lowering bindings, dispositions, selected-context admission and joint native execution. SOURCE_PATH-only semantic compilation is still present and must not be mistaken for complete selected-source coverage. The correspondence calculus, remaining overlap audit, separate O3/full-LTO measurements, both cold CI generations and full review/merge requirements all remain in the current plan.\n",
