.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1748-current.json:138:      "body": "Continued implementation in the C1 worktree, preserving the previous source inventory and correspondence changes (Principles 4, 7, 9, 17\u201319).\n\nThe compiler now reads ordinary statements, native RDF 1.2 reifier bindings and annotations through a shared default-graph boundary. It reuses PurRDF's ordinary indexes and subject-indexed native runs. Duplicate physical representations are deduplicated by exact indexed membership, without an accumulating seen set. Whole-source owned quad vectors have been replaced by streaming compiler/restriction passes, and common IRI remapping borrows the native spelling. No text round trip or second dataset is added. Unbound native probes still stream side tables; this is not a claim that every compiler analysis is fully indexed.\n\nNative-only inputs, structural declarations and modal variable discovery now use that same boundary. Bare quotation cannot become an unconditional assertion; named-graph metadata cannot supply default-graph scope. Invalid confidence, unknown modality, proposition-valued coordinates and unlowered coordinate multiplicity withhold the whole scoped axiom or rule with an error. Separate reifiers retain coexisting standpoints. Nested proposition lowering failures are explicit instead of panicking or silently stringifying. The compile stage identity is now `compile-logic.v16-native-statement-reads`.\n\nVerification on pinned nightly-2026-09-05:\n- 235/235 selected synthetic compiler/correspondence/restriction/source-catalog tests pass (nextest `216b3231-ff72-4090-90d2-97e6d25ace74`). Seven new semantic contracts; an existing invalid-confidence contract strengthened.\n- Workspace Clippy for libraries/tests/examples passes with `-D warnings`.\n- `make fmt` and `make lint` pass, including the corpus-producer seal.\n- The first new modal-constraint fixture lacked the mandatory guard; the production check rejected it, and the fixture was corrected. No check was weakened.\n\nNo corpus producer, full gate, PurRDF suite, commit, push or merge ran. Producer configuration remains O3/fat LTO/one codegen unit, separate from tests. Existing Cargo manifest/future-compatibility findings remain work to finish. Synthetic checks support no producer speedup claim.\n\nThe next concrete correspondence adapter defect is in `ingest/dataset.rs`: `DslView::reified_statements` and `annotation_*` still materialize owned records, scan the annotation table per lookup and match blank reifiers by label after discarding native scope. They must migrate to native scoped identity and indexed annotation runs; the adapter's empty-blank substitution for proposition objects also requires typed preservation/admission. This stays in the current correspondence implementation scope.\n\nThis update does not complete #1748 or #1741. Persistent all-family source-to-IR coverage, selected CompiledTheory, joint native program/DL closure, identical certified Reason/Verify execution, certified correspondence fusion/adoption, the remaining zero-overlap audit, separate O3 producer measurements, both independent cold CI generations and full gate/review/ghprsq merges remain required within the approved plan. Source reading and scope metadata are not execution certificates.\n",
