.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1748-current.json:153:      "body": "Implemented the next source-to-IR boundary in the existing correspondence worktree, preserving all prior work (Principles 4, 7, 9 and 17\u201319).\n\n- `PreparedLogicSource::compile_with_sources` returns immutable emission evidence borrowed from the exact prepared source. Runtime native IDs are not serialized or treated as durable certificates.\n- Ordinary and native annotation axioms carry their actual statement coordinates. Scoped claims carry their reifier roots. Restriction, enumeration and datarange expansion carries the original pre-skolemization root at emission.\n- Horn routing preserves each authored formula root. Axiom deduplication unions every contributing origin, including several authored formulas and an ordinary statement producing the same axiom. Scope remains part of the deduplication key.\n- Values and their origins undergo canonical sorting together exactly once; IR indices are assigned while detaching those paired values. No generated-IRI lookup, second lowering, RDF serialization or second source dataset is used to recover attribution.\n- Every declared formula gets an explicit outcome: axiom index, formula index, syntax read under an owner, malformed with its diagnostic index, or excluded by named-graph placement. Shared subtree failures retain every affected source root, even when diagnostics are deduplicated. Owner-bound syntax is not represented as globally asserted or executed.\n- `docs/PIPELINE_SPINE.md` documents this evidence boundary and its limits.\n\nValidation: `make fmt`, workspace Clippy (`--lib --tests --examples`, `-D warnings`) and `make lint` pass. `make nextest-synthetic` selected the compiler frontend, restriction, IR and projection families: **647/647 passed**, including seven new GMEOW lowering/ownership regressions. Nextest run `15b5b4cf-797b-4158-8c5c-8184a77b383e`; test compilation 3m04s, execution 0.178s. No corpus producer or upstream conformance suite ran, and no snapshot updates were needed. These are development checks, not O3/full-LTO producer measurements or a full gate. Existing Cargo manifest and proc-macro future-compatibility warnings remain plan work.\n\nThis does not close source coverage: all-family source/owner-to-IR bindings and dispositions remain required, including each consumed restriction/list statement, constraint sugar/UniqueLang, native schema/existential producers and selected obligations. Rules, contracts, correspondences and their owner execution still need complete accounting. The selected `CompiledTheory`, joint native execution, certified coverage/completion, production adoption and the full calculus remain current implementation scope. A source record, successful parse or bounded test corpus authorizes no unrestricted optimization rewrite. Zero upstream test overlap remains an unfinished audit. Both independent cold CI generations, producer measurements, full gates, current-head review and ghprsq merges remain required. Changes are uncommitted; no merge claimed.\n",
