.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1748-current.json:228:      "body": "The validation consumer now uses the same native source catalog and shared compiled theory as CompileLogic. This extends the existing implementation in the typed-correspondence worktree; it is still uncommitted and does not close this issue or the full calculus/production-adoption scope.\n\nThe source-construction audit confirms the exact scope: SourceLoad serializes `catalog.materialized()` into `pipeline/base-graph.nq`, before adding presentation, self-description and example graphs. That byte input includes root, module and import documents. Validation now borrows that same native dataset directly. The separate authored-only presentation graph is not substituted for it. The new declared parse-sources \u2192 validate edge and source-catalog receipt commitment are present in the owning ontology, Rust stage and executable full specification, with French/Chinese annotations for the new edge.\n\nBoth validation diagnostic folds consume the catalog's single compiled theory instead of reparsing and lowering the source independently. Gate category wiring now uses native indexed/default-graph statements rather than preparing and materializing a SPARQL SELECT result. Conflicting or non-IRI wiring remains fatal, native annotations participate, and a declared `logic:ruleGateFatalVerdict` that fails to lower cannot disappear into the no-rule case.\n\nThe substrate reconciliation A-Box is now a fixed borrowed graph/subject role view imported through PurRDF's native DatasetImporter. It preserves complete native terms, annotations and reifier bindings, excludes other provenance subjects and other graphs, and produces no RDF text intermediate or owned whole-provenance quad vector. It is a specific validation role, not a general graph-flattening certificate. Substrate inputs remain included in the authenticated SHACL input digest whenever that role contributes data. The source catalog lives through validation now: peak-memory effects need measurement; no memory or elapsed-time improvement is claimed from this code change alone.\n\nValidation passed: workspace Clippy with `-D warnings` (12.33s), formatting and managed lint; 22/22 final focused tests across 32 binaries, including the actual repository DAG/registry/full-spec parity test (build 1m09s, execution 0.016s). An earlier 23-test selection also passed; the separately added DAG parity check caught the missing executable-spec edge, which was fixed before the final run. Native-substrate evidence, gate wiring, malformed declared gate rejection, shared catalog ownership, SHACL diagnostic/advisory outputs and missing-reason-upstream failure are covered with synthetic inputs. No test reconstructed a repository corpus. Existing Cargo manifest and proc-macro-error2 future-compatibility warnings remain open.\n\nNo full producer/gate, dedicated i18n gate, cold-generation measurement, upstream PurRDF suite, commit, new PR or merge ran in this batch. Both independent cold CI generations remain required. Conversion/selection and shared diagnostic preparation have separate timing phases; the native selection reports zero serialized intermediate bytes. Full O3/fat-LTO elapsed/RSS/intermediate-byte experiments remain part of the plan.\n\nNext critical integration is the joint native reasoning run: the fixed `reason_all_certified` still omits the compiled program, while `reason_program_budgeted` combines ordinary rules then runs n-ary, DL/existential and modal augmentation sequentially. Replacing the entry point alone would not establish a joint fixed point, coherent budget, complete owner admission or a whole-source consistency proof. Shared native analyses, source/context coverage, joint producer scheduling, retained chase certificates/witnesses and authenticated portable run evidence remain required here. The test-ownership audit is also unfinished; no claim that 100% of PurRDF overlap has been removed. Principles 4, 7, 9, 17\u201319.\n",
