.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1748-current.json:243:      "body": "The correspondence worktree now has a native joint ordinary/existential executor, used by both `materialize_program` and `materialize_program_annotated`. This is implementation progress within the compiled-theory integration, not completion of this issue or of the whole-source consistency contract.\n\nThe native kernel prepares the combined predicate graph before running either family. Conjunctive heads share a stratum; termination certification sees ordinary feedback edges as well as existential producers. The shared indexed stores retain actual body facts, proof heights and provenance. Both producer families contribute to one canonical round commit under one global step governor across sorted worlds. A cut retains asserted facts from unrun worlds and under-claims the common completion frontier.\n\nThis removes the intermediate ordinary-closure-to-WorldStore rebuild and the separate unbudgeted existential post-pass from ordinary and annotated program materialization. Shared program preparations now lazily retain their immutable joint plan. Witness variable/frontier and reified tuple layouts are prepared once; positive existential triggers are revisited only when a body predicate changes. Selected annotations borrow contiguous world slices of the final native rows and fold the full joint run's physical lineage once, without rerunning joins or promoting derived facts to asserted seeds. The public materialization retains decomposable witness recipes; the structured existential entry uses the same native kernel.\n\nThe stratifier also accounts for the implicit math cell/type reads of dimension and bilinear builtins, freezing their producers before evaluation. Bound arithmetic filters do not invalidate finite-domain admission; arithmetic that publishes a generated head value still requires a range certificate for unbounded execution. This is a conservative admission boundary, not permission to drop an unsupported producer.\n\nValidation: the final main synthetic batch passed 56/56 tests. One additional native ordinary regression passed against the existing real four-worker fixture, comparing complete rows/provenance and every budget cut to forced sequential execution. Workspace Clippy and make lint passed after the final test addition. The public API tests exercise ordinary-to-nary-to-ordinary feedback, annotated lineage (four weight-3 tuple premises yield weight 81), shared budget cuts, and actual witness recipe retention. A separate regression proves that a dimension builtin waits for a produced type before emitting its violation. These are 57 focused GMEOW tests, not the full required gate. Existing Cargo manifest/future-compatibility warnings are not claimed resolved.\n\nThe full scope remains: bring the DL/schema and modal effects into the joint source-program run; retain and bind context, source coverage, completion, chase and witness evidence in the certified Reason/Verify result; consume that same run for obligations; authenticate portable restoration and installed-consumer receipts. `reason_program_budgeted` still has its old separate post-passes and is not yet the program-wide authority. General incremental rule/EDB reuse, full correspondence adoption, role projection, the remaining test ownership audit, and independent O3/full-LTO measurements remain required. Preserve both independent cold CI generations. No full producer/gate, upstream conformance run, performance claim, commit, push, PR or merge occurred for this batch. Principles 4, 7, 9, 17\u201319.\n",
