.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1748-current.json:303:      "body": "Canonical native preparation and matching are implemented and passed coordinated focused verification in the preserved integration worktree. All 171 selected tests passed, including ten new controls for canonical derived schema/marker feedback, exact variable/data identities, original premises, source-scope retention/refusal, negative cycles, list/chase matching and incomplete-producer frontiers. Native source identity includes the new resolver/store and namespace authority; prepared operator schema and solver identity were advanced. No authored corpus was produced by tests.\n\nThis reconciles the initial-only operator-adaptation defect: raw facts now retain their source spellings, while role-sensitive operator probes, signed dependencies, termination and completion use the declared interpretation. Original source scopes are retained before lowering, and unsupported standpoint/time/module/modality is refused by the explicit world-local template admission. This is not full scoped CompiledTheory execution.\n\nThe full current scope remains open: late DL/modal consequences must wake authored rules, derived schema and literal readers must share execution state, negative/universal decisions need complete-predecessor admission, and source ownership/coverage must govern production Reason, Verify and obligations. The ten-case audit remains the implementation checklist; do not treat this focused tranche or finite evidence as whole-source or unrestricted rewrite certification. Production correspondence optimization, ACT use cases, certified fusion and role projection remain prerequisites for parent completion.\n\nThe same 171-test batch validates native selected-blob fixture/validation adoption and report-only timing thresholds chosen explicitly instead of a fixed 2x floor. O3/full-LTO production measurements, all required gates and both independent cold CI generations still remain required. No new GMEOW commit or merge is claimed. Principles 4, 7, 9, 17\u201319.\n",
