.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1748-current.json:318:      "body": "### Native term and fact execution checkpoint\n\nThe native dictionary and every bound RelationStore probe now use exact PurRDF TermValue identity. IRI probes borrow their input; duplicate interning and bound joins allocate no display strings. Compiled constants are lowered once per shared plan. Display text is computed lazily at output. DAG leaf/free identity, compiled rule identity and witness frontiers reuse PurRDF's existing injective canonical encoding, preserving datatype, language, direction, blank scope and quoted components. Datatype value equality remains a separate logical operation. The planner is v18-native-term-probes.\n\nThe auxiliary FactStore now indexes the native fields already owned by each fact and has no duplicate rendered-key vector. Candidate keys, model comparison and stable-model intersections, annotations and negation consume native terms. Cost and parallel-execution evidence hashes use native canonical bytes. Public annotation text is rendered at its output boundary. The answer projector consumes the already-admitted goal, retains it for incremental queries, checks numeric constants and repeated variables with native equality, and renders only accepted bindings. This fixes numeric goal constraints previously being ignored. Annotated answers project each fact directly without allocating a one-row intermediate result vector.\n\nValidation: the broad native selection passed all 555 behavior/source controls (2m35s compilation, 0.801s execution); only the two expected old descriptor pins failed in that run. After refreshing those pins from the measured native contract, all 46 session/persistence/provenance/pin/source controls passed (0.143s execution). Producer-independent workspace Clippy passed with warnings denied (22.43s), and final Make lint passed every hook. Engine pin: 4babe087569cc3d50b613b29e9bd487c0f244baa35171d48cdd82ed0da7ac8f1. Fixed-session pin: 5b2150aed86743edcfe4a64393373939c602ca2e54590ee9c2cd9d86ad0ad286. These runs consume only independent synthetic GMEOW inputs; no authored corpus was produced by a test.\n\nThese controls exercise GMEOW's term admission, dictionaries, DAG lowering, witnesses, rule/model semantics and answer projection; they add no duplicate PurRDF conformance suite. PurRDF's repository and branches remain untouched. The O3/full-LTO/one-codegen-unit producer, enabled assertions/overflow checks, separate test lineage and both independent cold CI generation definitions were rechecked and retained. Their actual full production/CI execution is still required. There is no numerical speedup claim.\n\nWhole-source native model/context ownership, correspondence/ACT execution and certified composition/fusion/role adoption, authentic producer/public-CLI/browser verification, separate O3/full-LTO resource measurements, the full gate and protected finalization remain required within the existing plan. No whole-plan completion, commit, push or merge is claimed. Principles 4, 7, 17\u201319.\n\n### Preserved integration evidence\n\nCurrent integration remains in `.worktrees/issue-1741-typed-correspondence`, base `f9c3e6307fb1c5ae861dc02483de73856ab89832`. All prior dirty work and the separate producer/fixture candidates are preserved. PurRDF remains with its assigned agent; no upstream branch, worktree or repository was modified.\n\nNative bundle/fixture adoption uses one selected-blob import on a cold miss, shares the dataset Arc with action publication and artifact consumers, and admits warm receipts without restoring a dataset. Prepared shapes, archives, envelope heads, verification laws and flat validation consume authenticated inputs. Native terms, scoped blanks, quoted statements, literal value interpretations, worlds and premises retain their existing exact identities. The source Arc plus consequence delta still avoids cumulative carrier materialization. Typed cache payload schema 13, typed-payload4, reason.v9-typed-closure-objects and validate.v11-typed-reasoned-input retain their invalidation contracts.\n\nNative scheduling now includes complete-input value flow for ordinary, atomic existential and schema/list producers. Every relevant native constant has its own abstract cell; Other covers every remaining value. Every selected fact contributes to the source summary. Positive binding intersections and a monotone producer closure narrow effects conservatively; forgotten world/tuple correlations, ignored guards and TOP generated variables can add possible firings but cannot remove concrete firings. No sampling or data-selected predicate shortcut certifies absence. The immutable borrowed JointInput binds the complete abstract shape and source template through admission and execution. Changed values under unchanged predicates invalidate the plan when dependencies change; equal abstract shapes reuse preparation while executing their actual native values and worlds. Ordinary strata consume the shared signed producer certificate instead of repeating isolated stratification. Last-writer completion, including unknown predicate writers, remains mandatory.\n\nImmutable templates share ordinary join layouts and exact rule keys, existential witness/frontier layouts, and prepared schema/list layouts across different input-dependent strata. Regrouping stores rule indices rather than cloning/lowering the rules again. The opaque certificate checks the cached exact rule keys; a same-name different rule cannot acquire its authority. An executable's head inventory includes only its selected indices. Schema termination abstraction copies only proof terms and never mutates executable layouts. The redundant joint-stratum process cache is removed: bounded source-template and admitted-plan caches own reuse, and dropping their last consumer releases the layouts instead of leaving a hidden retention path.\n\nFurther DL contradictions now participate in the shared authored-rule fixed point: negative property assertion records (both target forms), disjoint-property value collisions, marker- and canonical-record functionality, asymmetric/irreflexive property clashes, and explicit equality/distinctness clashes with sameAs symmetry/transitivity. Their native datatype guards reuse the existing exact DL/refutation interpretation without constructing or parsing an RDF surface. Pure comparisons add no hidden statement reads. Every operand must be bound; undefined datatype mappings fail explicitly. Different resource names alone do not prove functional distinctness. One per-world cache shares interpretations across strata/rounds, retaining at most 128 literals with at most 8KiB source payload each; misses and oversized inputs compute identical semantics without retention. Every conclusion carries its actual schema/value/identity premises, and these conclusions now wake authored consumers before any terminal DL augmentation. This is not a claim that the remaining DL augmentation has been replaced.\n\nNative key clashes now also execute inside the same shared fixed point. Complete nonempty RDF-list keys and canonical KeyAssertion records both join their native property values without rendering/parsing RDF or materializing a product of intermediate joins. Every component retains one actual agreeing value pair and the complete definition, class and explicit-distinctness evidence. Thing keys require no separately asserted Thing membership. Canonical keyClass/keyProperty writers must complete before agreement: adding a component can invalidate an earlier agreement without making the record malformed, so those reads are strict signed dependencies while value matches remain positive. A feedback cycle through a key definition is refused. List and record definitions share one bounded round cache with distinct entry kinds (64 entries/256KiB total); datatype meanings keep their existing per-world bounded reuse. Legacy coverage now accumulates canonical class/property sets and withholds malformed records instead of silently choosing one class or discarding invalid fields, including when there are no candidate individuals. LOGIC-IR states the completion and evidence contract. These are native key-clash guards, not a claim that general equality substitution or every key entailment is complete.\n\nNative maximum/exact-upper-bound contradictions now feed the authored-rule fixed point too. Immutable CardinalityPattern layouts select all values, object resources, an explicit class, or an explicit datatype expression. Each bound stays conjunctive; qualified maxima never guess a missing qualifier. The native operator uses indexed property/type/inequality rows, compact local candidate IDs and one backtracking path to find maximum+1 provably distinct fillers. It does not materialize combinations or assume that different resource names denote distinct individuals. Every conclusion retains the bound, restriction, property, qualifier and actual value/inequality evidence. Literal value equality shares NativeValues; late values, class memberships and explicit inequalities participate through positive signed reads and an implicit delta pivot. Undefined datatype semantics cannot become a negative decision, while unrelated opaque values cannot hide an independent witnessed overflow. Counts stay u128 until bounded by the finite candidate inventory, so large counts do not truncate or allocate by source magnitude. A separate 128-entry/8KiB-per-source count cache reuses the projection's explicit lexical-count convention and PurRDF's typed integer/subtype validation. Supported named XSD membership delegates to PurRDF; exact rational and language/direction residue use the shared native interpretations. Datatype-expression compilation now shares the native store and completed definitions as described below; minimum-bound witnesses remain required integration work. Key agreement now probes exact native identity through Bound::Both before comparing cross-lexical literal values, avoiding resource-value cross-product scans. LOGIC-IR records the positive maximum-witness contract. Planner identity: gmeow-native-plan-v15-direct-chase-publication, including the native chase changes recorded below. Identity readback exposed a pre-existing omission: the native hash folded the refutation registry but omitted its datatype/counting/case-split family sources. All three registered family modules now participate explicitly, so edits to those implementations invalidate old checkpoints and cached certificates.\n\nFinite datatype expressions now compile directly from each world's native store to an immutable topologically ordered DAG. Named spaces, literal enumerations, union, intersection, complement and ordered/length restrictions share native value interpretations. Every distinct conjunctive facet is retained, including repeated fields on one carrier. Compilation retains actual constructor/list/facet premises. Intrinsic redefinitions, multiple constructor values, incomplete/cyclic lists or expression DAGs, unordered facet operands and unsupported facets fail explicitly. Complement is value-space negation, never missing-RDF-fact negation. Constructor/list/facet reads are Completed signed dependencies; their producers finish before a cardinality witness can use the definition, and feedback cycles through those definitions are refused. Value relations stay positive and can grow in later rounds. Each world owns one 64-entry/512KiB plan cache across its strata/rounds; misses and oversized plans execute without retention. Shared child nodes lower once without recursive tree expansion. Named membership consumes the already interpreted input; enumerands are interpreted once during compilation, so large operands are not reparsed for every probe. The proof keeps their original lexical source facts. LOGIC-IR records this finite-definition admission/evidence contract. The datatype refutation scanner now uses this same compiler. A world-local native store replaces its legacy recursive datatype/value hierarchy; a bounded inventory shares inherited restriction/property pairs across individuals (64 classes / 256KiB payload), and currently unreachable definitions still require admission; no RDF text conversion occurs during source admission, definition lowering, value comparison or inherited proof traversal. One lazy source analysis supplies all datatype queries within the coverage pass. A retained plan computes its capacity lazily once; nested restrictions lower their full facet chain to one PurRDF primitive operation without separately lowering every prefix. Exact rational/real/decimal interval bounds and enumeration identity use the shared native values. Unknown capacities, unsupported facets and incomplete definitions remain explicit refusals. Range/allValuesFrom constrain existing values; each someValuesFrom requests its own witness, and every qualified minimum/exact count requires its explicit onDataRange. Repeated lower/exact/facet fields stay conjunctive. A large source count remains u128 through its structured proof and never sizes an allocation. Every asserted datatype-property value is inspected, including named ranges and the literal-only property contract. Unmodeled class/property obligations and uninterpreted enumeration members cannot acquire a whole-case consistency certificate. Clashes retain actual world-local inherited paths, definitions, bounds and violating values. General intersected/qualified value-space models and upper-bound consistency still require their joint native ownership. The native contradiction producers below now feed their stated datatype consequences into the authored fixed point.\n\nThe finite-datatype math projection assertion moved from an unauthenticated source-parsing unit test into the existing authenticated math consumer group. Its producer reuses the original native math parse, publishes every collected count/datatype field, and keys the changed mandatory observation with source-only-math-lowering-v3-datatype-inventory and gmn-grounding-v5-datatype-inventory. The consumer compares distinct parsed count values, rejects malformed/conflicting fields, requires unique datatype owners, and compares every authored finite capacity to the same native datatype-capacity API used by execution. PurRDF primitive finite capacities are retained directly; the parallel one-entry Rust count table is deleted. No corpus was generated by a test; the authenticated consumer still awaits the required producer run.\n\nNative datatype contradictions now also execute as typed operations in the shared fixed point. PropertyOperation makes list, cardinality and datatype operations mutually exclusive; prepared layouts mirror that choice and validate bound operands once. DatatypeConstraint handles literal-domain violations, actual membership failures and insufficient capacity for a required lower count. It shares the world's RelationStore, compiled DatatypePlan, list cache and NativeValues; its witness borrows the plan's original definition premises without an intermediate dataset or proof-vector clone. Literal-domain checks have no hidden reads. Membership/capacity depend on completed constructors, lists and facets; operands are ordinary positive joins, so no extra definition delta pivot or repeated lowering is needed. Undefined membership/capacity refuses execution explicitly. Schema selectors bind before indexed instance/value probes; leaf membership needs no temporary expression-results vector. PurRDF primitive capacity results are retained in full, including finite Boolean capacity previously discarded. Primitive conformance is upstream-owned; the new GMEOW control checks that the resulting contradiction reaches an authored consumer.\n\nThe fixed native laws cover declared datatype-property literal-only contracts, property and local universal memberships, empty existential fillers, explicit qualified minimum/exact capacities, and minimum/exact/existential requests constrained by an independently insufficient universal range. Qualified counts require onDataRange, repeated fields are conjunctive, and independent existential fillers remain separate. All conclusions retain actual source spellings, worlds, definitions, counts and value evidence. This is positive contradiction production; it does not claim complete datatype model or minimum/exact witness generation.\n\nThe complete native registry agreement has moved out of a full-module source-parsing unit test into the existing authenticated pipeline consumer group. NativeFragmentRegistry exposes the kernel's exact pattern, decided-fragment, deciding-pattern, completeness-bound, boundary and reason inventory. The producer collects those six mandatory fields from its existing native source dataset using borrowed quads/terms; ambiguous or invalid pattern targets and characterizations fail. Exact struct equality preserves every previous bidirectional check, including stray entries. A compact artifact export binds the original parent receipt once, so consumers do not repeatedly restore/authenticate the large parent product. Conformance version is conformance.v12-complete-native-registry. The authored datatype completeness characterization now names native definition and primitive upper-bound evidence instead of the deleted table. These descriptive registries do not authorize optimization rewrites.\n\nFinal verification: all 831 selected native/synthetic tests passed (1m14s build, 9.517s execution); producer-independent workspace Clippy passed with warnings denied (9.12s), and every make lint hook passed. The prior production-source run passed every new datatype and registry control; it exposed one previously unselected synthetic receipt setup error alongside the two stale engine pins. The receipt test now explicitly selects its tiny artifact before using its commitment, retaining every parent/artifact tampering rejection. Both unreleased native.2 identity pins were deliberately refreshed for v13. Twelve datatype-producer integration controls cover actual canonical/projection spellings, lexical evidence, local/universal membership, independent existentials, facet premises, repeated/large/qualified counts, no qualifier guessing, empty spaces, late definition completion, feedback-cycle refusal, world locality, upstream finite capacity reaching an authored consumer, and explicit unknown interpretation/capacity refusal. The existing native scheduling, keys, maximum witnesses, modal, provenance, source-inventory and compact receipt controls remain green. Three synthetic registry-observation controls passed. The authenticated full-source registry/math assertions still require the genuine producer run.\n\nEvidence: .cache/agentic-plan/datatype-producer-{tests-final,clippy-verified,lint-final}.log, datatype-producer-registry-tests.log and datatype-producer-verified-sources.sha256 (35 checked files). No source changed after final verification and no owned builder remains running. These are focused integration checks: no full producer, authenticated corpus consumer run, full gate or optimized producer measurement is claimed.\n\nRequired implementation remains #1704/#1748: complete native source-identity closure and remaining datatype model/refutation adoption into the authored joint fixed point, minimum/exact existential and remaining refutation/modal producers plus key/equality entailments; refresh structural analyses as their dependencies change; preserve the selected model/entailment and equality contracts; include all existential effects in joint termination admission; derive modal absence/universality authority from actual producer/SCC completion. Modal assertion context, evaluation world and typed accessibility remain distinct. Positive possibility witnesses and completion-dependent failure/universality outputs require their actual signed dependencies. Complete selected CompiledTheory context/source admission and production Reason/Verify/obligation ownership, and remove the remaining duplicated schema execution and program -> DL -> modal sequencing. The native guarded, key and maximum laws establish direct feedback for their stated operations, not completion of that full execution model.\n\nFull correspondence execution, both ACT use cases, certified composition/fusion and certified role projection under #1737 remain required implementation scope. Production correspondence optimization still blocks #1738. Every logical check and both independent cold CI generations remain mandatory. Conversion removal, fusion, incremental reuse and scheduling each need elapsed-time, peak-memory and intermediate-byte observations on the O3/full-LTO/1CGU producer; no historical speedup or fixed improvement bar is required. Finite examples never authorize unrestricted rewrites. The 41 authenticated corpus tests and genuine bundle/four embedding-consumer builds remain required. No repository corpus producer was invoked for this verification and no fabricated fixture credentials were supplied. Small source-fixture refutation sweeps still require resolution in the continuing authenticated-corpus ownership audit; the passing static seal alone does not establish exhaustive producer purity. The current ownership audit records 47 removed duplicate tests and 5 removed generic fuzz targets. Read-only inspection of PurRDF at 77fe898ce925023b214818232f30a425ecb83bed found no OntoUML parser/metamodel adapter in crates/: the retained GMEOW OntoUML tests exercise its own model interpretation, canonical lowering and native foundation verdicts. Upstream generic format/SHACL/XSD conformance remains upstream; no upstream suite was run. A repository-wide zero-overlap claim is not yet established. No full GMEOW gate, commit or merge is claimed. Principles 4, 7, 9, 17\u201319.\n\n### Producer ownership and native observation checkpoint\n\nA further producer-ownership batch is implemented locally and remains uncommitted in the preserved worktree. Native isolated-refutation and repeated-kernel corpus execution, CLIF ingestion, glossary coordinates, epistemics instance probes, and the complete GMN vector corpus now have authenticated producer observations. Selected native operations share one lazy input parse and have separate bounded action keys. CLIF evidence retains typed quads, worlds, annotation certificates and direct lineage. Epistemics retains its complete class universe, actual closure size and selected instance rows without storing the unchanged module five times. No finite observation authorizes unrestricted correspondence rewrites.\n\nThe full GMN 19-positive/8-negative inventory shares the producer's native dictionary; positive observation/grading is shared with the CLI. CLI codebook loading now hydrates the existing produced native packet. Its ten conformance dispatch tests use independent small user inputs; full authored-vector and ring assertions remain producer-observation consumers. One redundant RL nonempty smoke test was removed because its product assertions are already stronger in the retained norm-claims bundle consumer.\n\n**Verified:** producer-independent workspace Clippy with warnings denied; 846/846 selected synthetic native/cache/transport tests (final build 1.20 s, execution 7.745 s); final managed lint and the supported source-flow scanner. Complete native term transport now participates in both engine identity inventories, and the engine/session descriptor pins were refreshed only after their source-participation tests passed. The first broader filter accidentally selected a real-corpus consumer; it correctly failed closed without any supplied/generated fixture. The final filter names the three independent action controls explicitly. This is focused evidence, not a full gate or a producer-performance claim.\n\n**Still required inside this plan:** complete ownership audit, real authenticated corpus consumption, and compilation/execution of the changed CLI against genuine produced artifacts. The source-backed CLI backward/migration repairs are now implemented as recorded below. The producer-independent checks exclude the four genuine-bundle consumer packages; the newly changed CLI tests have not yet run. Both cold CI generations, separate resource measurements, full correspondence/deontic/native/prover integration and protected finalization remain required. No full gate, new commit or merge is claimed. PurRDF is untouched. Parent #1704 now records upstream PurRDF #281 completed, while downstream #1732/#1745 adoption remains open.\n\n\n### CLI ownership checkpoint\n\nThe remaining identified CLI authored-source paths have been repaired locally. Backward and migration dispatch tests use independent small user inputs; fragment readers consume the actual produced bundle. Complete authored demonstrator expectations remain in authenticated pipeline consumers. Default migration dictionary loading now hydrates the existing native packet. Public export/projection tests use tiny user snapshots instead of regenerating the whole corpus.\n\nThe expanded lexical seal follows authored paths through command arguments and helper returns; its regression controls and repository scan pass. It exposed a developer query test that silently succeeded if its real corpus directory was absent; this now uses a single explicit-world user fact and rule. The developer whole-snapshot projection smoke test was removed because that command is optimized-producer-only. Its admission requirement is checked without dispatch, while successful output/view contracts remain covered by public CLI and native projection tests.\n\nProducer-independent Clippy with warnings denied passes. Four focused developer query/admission tests pass (14.58-second build, 0.009-second execution). Final managed lint passes all hooks, and seven source SHA-256s are unchanged after lint. Initial incomplete-world and producer-admission failures are retained in the evidence ledger. The changed public CLI still requires genuine producer artifacts before it can compile/run. This is not a full producer/gate or an exhaustive zero-overlap claim. All existing native/deontic/prover/correspondence/ACT scope, both cold CI generations, separate resource observations and protected finalization remain required. PurRDF is untouched. Principles 4, 7, 17\u201319.\n\n\n### Native chase publication checkpoint\n\nRestricted-chase body joins and conjunctive head probes now traverse indexed native cursors while retaining only the current binding path. A complete head extension stops the existence probe immediately; an unfinished search cannot establish absence or invent a witness. Bound native-term inequalities prune partial paths without adding a DL unique-name assumption. Actual body premises and source spellings survive. The physical-source census now recurses through every nested module and explicitly classifies forward-only and test-only files; no new nested module can escape classification.\n\nGrounded chase heads now publish directly into the existing joint candidate buffer with borrowed firing premises. This removes a second pending-row vector, intermediate premise copies, and reifier hashes that the joint path previously discarded and recomputed. Standalone publication retains its original first-source proof in a FactKey-ordered map and computes source reifiers lazily once per needed firing. Joint publication retains its existing total provenance ordering. Raw-candidate ceilings, whole-conjunction handling, witness recipes, world identity, completed predicates and the shared derivation governor remain mandatory. New controls cover late selective joins, exact-cap completion, actual source retention, repeated variables, early conjunctive blocking, unfinished-search withholds, duplicate-head budget behavior and competing joint proofs in reversed producer order.\n\nProducer-independent workspace Clippy passed with warnings denied (22.05 seconds). All 850 selected behavior/source controls passed (2m21s build, 7.659s execution); the only initial failures were the two intentionally stale descriptor pins. After source participation passed, both updated pins passed their focused rerun. Managed lint passed every hook. Nine final source hashes record this batch; no production source changed between its behavioral checks and pin refresh. The engine descriptor is b9c65eb635bc20b7856016a8b75cbf9638b9543061d76d547ad8d93ec2cc5534.\n\nThe consolidated make check completed unsuccessfully after 1346.351 seconds (22m26s), including a successful O3/full-LTO producer build of 20m47s. Lint passed. Synchronization failed before corpus execution because the hand-built sink dependency list was not normalized as the RDF loader expects. Crate/source checks reported 140 findings: 129 string-error violations across live caches and serialized observations, ten stale interactive-engine attestations, and one obsolete correspondence-lowering GTS authorship declaration. Dependent gates did not run, and the public CLI remains uncompiled. Exact logs and task/resource timings are retained; this run did not measure whole-run peak RSS.\n\nThe post-gate repair batch now normalizes dependency sets at the StageSpec constructor and tests complete-plan binding without executing any stage. The obsolete GTS authorship declaration is removed. All 129 first-party string-error violations are resolved: live errors preserve typed sources and context; serializable observation records preserve the complete reachable diagnostic causal closure without becoming executable certificates. Successful native preparations are reused; a failed initialization publishes no cached action and cannot trigger an automatic retry. Both observation codecs are versioned for the new records. GMEOW diagnostics select the exact pinned purrdf-core package, and xtask no longer reaches the unused logic compiler. Cargo metadata verifies both now reach only the upstream core/cdt/events/iri/xsd packages. No upstream tests were run.\n\nThe producer-independent selection ran 986 checks: 984 behavior/source controls passed, and only two intentionally stale identity pins failed. After their measured refresh, both pins and four action/cache controls passed a six-test rerun (1m32s compilation, 0.012-second execution). Final managed lint passes all hooks. Final workspace Clippy passes with warnings denied (37.68 seconds). Resolved Cargo artifact profiles confirm O3, zero debug symbols, enabled assertions and overflow checks for GMEOW errors, pipeline and developer CLI; project configuration now prevents the host dev-profile setting from reintroducing symbols. The source/static checker confirms the original 129 string-error findings and obsolete GTS declaration are gone. Exactly ten findings remain, all stale browser-engine attestations across query, validate, GMN and reason. These require genuine normal-target rebuilds; GMN and validate first require authenticated producer artifacts. The earlier O3/full-LTO producer is stale and will not be used for admitted production. The full gate and public CLI are still unverified on this batch.\n\nThe query and reason browser engines have now been genuinely rebuilt and re-vendored against the exact pinned PurRDF revision. Query passed seven fresh-package Node checks, its Rust asset audit and nine shipped-copy Node checks. Reason refreshed its verified proof/counterproof witness, passed all four Node parity checks and its Rust asset audit. The reviewed 100-statement conjecture witness retains both outcomes and the same counterproof premises; changes reflect native.2 identities and native premise ordering. The query refresh now checks the fresh package before copying and the shipped copy after manifest production, so an interrupted refresh can recover without depending on its stale old digest. Every existing package check remains required. Initial failures and successful recovery are retained, including the pinned toolchain disappearing during the first verifier compilation and being restored to the exact nightly.\n\nTwo remaining tests that asserted only Turtle parser success/failure were removed, along with the parser-only assertion in the OntoUML observation test. GMEOW sameAs policy, native discipline/world/unsupported judgments, and contextual orchestration error checks remain. No upstream conformance suite ran. Final managed lint passes. The rebuilt source checker now reports exactly four findings: stale GMN and validation browser attestations in the site and mdbook views. Both require genuine producer-authenticated bundle/codebook artifacts before their normal refresh targets can execute. No current full-gate pass, public-CLI verification, exhaustive zero-overlap audit or merge is claimed.\n\n### Native object-witness integration checkpoint\n\nLocal native execution now handles compact qualified minimum/exact object-witness families, declared unqualified object bounds and some-values obligations in the shared authored-rule fixed point. Witnesses retain their asserting world, every body-bound frontier argument and actual source premises. Counts never expand the executable template. Checked arithmetic bounds a complete firing before witness allocation; required property/type/inequality rows publish directly to the shared candidate buffer. The native distinct-subset search distinguishes found, absent and exhausted. An unfinished search cannot authorize invention or completion, and a one-witness presence probe stops at the first qualifying existing value without materializing the rest of its relation.\n\nTermination admission shares the complete native value-flow analysis. Immutable definition bindings can specialize analysis directly; finite derived selector domains use the same abstract interpreter with at most 512 exact value cells, retaining Other for every possible future value. Every finite binding combination participates, with bounded enumeration and metadata. Selector values are borrowed from their shared native cells rather than copied into per-variable payload inventories. No concrete intermediate closure, RDF serialization or second rule lowering is used. Compact two-ordinal witness families authorize only the position-based weak-acyclicity proof: they cannot stand in for arbitrary nonlinear tuple joins in the stronger critical-instance analyses. Native binary relations are retained when selectors fix every predicate. Three-distinct-sibling recursion, mutable/ambiguous definitions and changed-source cache reuse are covered by refusal controls. Joint certificates carry an input contract; the cache key observes every actual source fact/world because enriched value cells can distinguish formerly unknown dynamic-predicate values. No bounded run authorizes an unrestricted rewrite.\n\nValidation: 181 behavior/source checks passed in the broad native selection. After replacing per-variable selector payload copies with borrowed native cells, 26 targeted controls passed; only the two expected stale descriptor pins remained. Both measured pins were refreshed for planner v16, and the final five-test pin/source-inventory run passes. Workspace Clippy passes with warnings denied (28.85 seconds), and the final managed lint run passes every hook. The controls include finite unbudgeted inheritance, world/provenance preservation, changed-source cache refusal, multiple or mutable definitions, three-sibling recursion, huge-count allocation refusal, incomplete-search refusal, and the 256-existing-values/eight-step presence fast path. These are independent synthetic GMEOW inputs; tests never produce the authored corpus.\n\nThe previously rebuilt producer and reason browser witness/attestation predate this semantic batch and must be regenerated against the final native contract. The earlier four-only source-finding count is historical evidence, not a current source check. GMN/validation refresh still requires producer-authenticated artifacts. No full gate, current public-CLI verification, exhaustive zero-overlap claim, commit, push or merge is claimed. PurRDF and its branches remain untouched; no upstream conformance suite ran. This completes a bounded native object-witness integration batch, not whole-source model ownership or the remaining joint semantic scope.\n\nSeparate producer resource measurements, both independent cold CI generations, complete native minimum/exact and datatype model ownership, deontic/modal integration, full correspondence/ACT execution and certified fusion/role projection, prover feedback and protected finalization remain required within the current plan. These changes do not claim an exhaustive zero-overlap audit or a numerical speedup. PurRDF remains untouched. Principles 4, 7, 17\u201319.\n\n### Native equality and producer conversion checkpoint\n\nThe shared native fixed point now publishes deterministic resource equalities from functionality, inverse functionality and maximum/exact-one object restrictions, plus both directions of local hasSelf restrictions. Canonical characteristic records and direct markers retain their actual premises. Native literal comparisons and count guards reuse the existing bounded value caches. Resource names are preserved; larger maxima never choose an arbitrary equality. Ten new independent GMEOW controls cover authored-rule feedback, late values, lexical evidence, qualification, world/input reuse, explicit contradictions, unknown comparisons, budget exhaustion and boolean flags. This does not yet complete general congruence, key entailment or whole-source model ownership.\n\nThe production reason stage now projects each derived axiom once into its required Turtle and native carrier through one shared traversal. Complete proof annotations, world evidence, receipt identities, modal claim status and math-expression identity edges survive both outputs. Anonymous proof scopes are disjoint from existing/source blanks, including nested quotes and composite-literal blanks; duplicate proof occurrences remain separate. The final native carrier is frozen once and shared directly by the product. Closure Turtle re-parsing and the intermediate frozen closure are removed. Witness heads resolve once, serve certificate links, and publish directly into native diagnostics, deleting their N-Triples serialization/parsing. The separate diagnostics-report RDF adapter remains; this is not a claim that every conversion is gone. Stage metadata records removed closure reparse bytes, zero closure parses/intermediate freezes, one witness projection pass and zero witness wire bytes independently of required artifacts. The reason stage receipt version is reason.v10-native-closure-projection.\n\nValidation is complete for this batch: all 217 selected native/producer controls pass, including both measured contract pins and source inventories (3m19s compilation, 0.755s execution). This includes GMEOW wire/native proof agreement, duplicate proof and quoted/existing blank isolation, native carrier reuse, modal evidence and witness/certificate links. Producer-independent workspace Clippy passes with warnings denied (51.83 seconds); final managed lint passes every hook. Planner v17-equality-and-local-self pins engine 94609bc5e09d2fbc2fb0c15321d9a35d4cf0adfce3513f72738368ca65b00b0b and fixed session 604003f0412162819a90722e22bb76a03c70d5ec6ef356352397a5904a81b420. The exact already-pinned purrdf-core dependency supplies composite-literal blank ownership; no upstream repository or branch was changed and no upstream tests ran.\n\nThe full gate, optimized producer/browser refresh, authentic corpus/public-CLI acceptance, separate O3/full-LTO resource measurements, both independent cold CI generations, exhaustive overlap audit, remaining native model/context and correspondence/ACT integration, and protected finalization remain required in this plan. Both cold CI generations and producer profile settings were rechecked and retained. No numerical speedup, full completion, commit, push or merge is claimed. Principles 4, 7, 17\u201319.\n",
