.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1748-current.json:348:      "body": "Native reduce execution is implemented in the preserved correspondence worktree under this plan (Principles 4, 7, 17 and 19).\n\nCanonical COUNT/SUM/AVG/MIN/MAX rules now retain a validated typed operator through lowering, shared preparation and native plan identity. Execution calls PurRDF's existing value-level fold API directly: no generated SPARQL, RDF round trip or temporary dataset. Group membership is the set of full body substitutions within a world, so equal values from different members remain distinct. Guards run before grouping. Result/group/input scope and bound negation are checked before admission.\n\nThe shared producer graph requires complete predecessors for every reduce read, including ordinary, existential and schema writers. Strict cycles are refused even without negation. Source-sensitive analyses conservatively retain empty-group and generated-value effects. A predecessor budget cut cannot publish a partial count. Reductions contribute finite seeds to later strata rather than masquerading as recursive existential variables.\n\nMaterialization explicitly requires StratifiedNAFProfile. Certification consumes the same strict dependency proof. Ordinary annotations use the declared CompleteGroupSupport / StratifiedAggregate contract; joint existential execution uses StratifiedAggregateChase and selected physical lineage. Explicitly selected worlds survive a probe with no relevant rows. LOGIC-IR documents grouping, empty results, undefined folds, witness selection and annotation semantics. Engine and plan identity cover the new operators and selected-world behavior.\n\nThis is execution infrastructure for the required authored correspondence-axis rules, not completion of those rules or a fusion theorem. Source arithmetic/t-norm/model declarations, complete selected-source coverage, the remaining optics/complements/transactions, ACT cases, certified fusion and role projection, and production adoption remain current implementation scope. The ordinary signed circuit and Gelfond-Lifschitz reduct cannot erase an aggregate; the session reports the supported full-native rebuild route explicitly.\n\nValidation: all 141 selected checks are verified across batched runs. The expanded run passed 138; two intentional engine/session pin changes and a test that incorrectly expected a separate Skolem recipe per world were resolved in a final 4/4 run, including the engine source inventory. The corrected test asserts distinct world facts/scores with the existing rule+frontier recipe identity. Ten new GMEOW reduction cases cover grouping, complete writers, cuts, cycles, empty selected worlds, profile admission, cache identity, bound negation, annotation lineage, joint existential execution and session routing. Earlier 91/91 focused checks also passed. Strict workspace-feature Clippy passed (33.13s), repository lint passed, and explicit lint of all three new source files passed. Tests had corpus-selector credentials removed; no upstream conformance suite ran. A 93-source manifest binds this verified local state. No corpus producer, full gate, commit, push or merge has run in this batch. The existing CI fixture integration and both independent cold generation definitions are preserved. PurRDF is untouched; Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf#286 remains open at the latest read. Separate O3/full-LTO producer observations for conversion/fusion/incremental/scheduling remain required, with elapsed time, peak memory and intermediate bytes and no invented minimum speedup.\n",
