.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1748-current.json:378:      "body": "The current native audit resolves an earlier witness-identity assumption against the normative logic design. `LOGIC-IR` requires source formula, binding, world/context and governing contract in witness identity. The earlier checkpoint that accepted one rule/frontier recipe across worlds does not satisfy that requirement. This is required implementation under this issue and #1704, not a compatibility contract to retain.\n\nThe coherent implementation sequence is:\n\n1. Give generic existential and minimum-family producers one typed scoped witness address. Retain each committed minting head, its actual witness position and world. Publication must consume those records directly: the current object-only closure search can fail on subject-only witnesses or choose an unrelated later edge. Remove that heuristic and the world-independent address, preserving the shared governor and honest budget prefixes.\n2. Admit source-owned EDB existential definitions directly from the native statement tables with exact source graph, blank scope, literals, declaration/slot evidence and complete body/head identity. Deduplicate identical RDF assertions, reject conflicting/missing slots, and never blanket-normalize data IRIs. Scope execution by source ownership and include the complete producer set in bounded preparation/cache identities and shared effects/termination analysis.\n3. For an immutable-definition profile, prove that selected producers cannot change rule declarations or slots; otherwise refuse that profile explicitly. Supporting generated definitions requires their declared completed producer boundary before preparation. A snapshot that silently ignores newly derived rules is not an implementation.\n4. Add a non-empty object-domain obligation only for explicitly admitted contexts/contracts, reusing bodyless native existential execution. Its origin is the typed intrinsic domain contract, not a fabricated reflexive RDF premise. Do not infer logical domains from every carrier/import/IR graph. Exact top-subclass rules must handle both declared Thing spellings in their class roles without aliasing arbitrary subjects/data. Ordinary shared laws then derive the local consequences before dependent absence claims.\n5. Retain exact source/contract/world and minting-head evidence through native results, explanations, receipts and the production carrier. The old terminal reasoning pass can be removed only after this and the remaining source/modal/refutation interactions are completely admitted on the shared path.\n\nThe empty-property audit also confirms that OWL bottom-property IRIs are not declared canonical vocabulary aliases; no invented `logic:` bottom aliases are authorized.\n\nA related consumer repair is now in source: the native verdict and unsatisfiable-class fold share role-sensitive canonical/projected matching, and validation locates evidence by exact subject, world and membership-versus-subsumption role. A data predicate merely mentioning Nothing cannot become or supply a clash. Documentation is being moved from reparsed closure Turtle to its mandatory existing typed Reasoning handle. These source changes have not yet passed compiled checks.\n\nRequired controls include selected/foreign/empty worlds, source-content and contract identity changes, reordering stability, annotation-only definitions, conflicting slots, quoted non-assertion, cross-world rule isolation, definition writers, cross-producer invention cycles, subject-only/multi-head publication and budget-cut prefixes. Tests use tiny independent GMEOW inputs or exact authenticated producer observations; no test produces the authored corpus or repeats upstream conformance. Full source coverage, both independent cold CI generations, separate O3/full-LTO resource measurements and the full gate remain required. Principles 4, 7, 9, 17\u201319.\n",
