.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:1:# Issue #1768: feat: add a first-class consumer prover entry point
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:2:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:3:State: OPEN   Repo: Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-ontology   Forge: github
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:4:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:5:## Body
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:6:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:7:## Problem
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:8:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:9:GMEOW has a capable native prover and a TPTP projection, but a consumer currently has to understand the internal `logic:Formula` / `logic:relation` / indexed `logic:TermCarrier` encoding to make an assertion visible to proof. #1755 demonstrated the failure mode: plausible domain triples are accepted as RDF but never enter the logical carrier, so an intended obligation can be silently unenforced.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:10:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:11:We need one obvious installed-binary path for asking GMEOW to prove a claim. This is a public consumer operation under the CLI razor: it must work from `gmeow` plus the embedded `gmeow.gts`, with no repository checkout or developer pipeline.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:12:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:13:## Scope
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:14:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:15:Add a first-class `gmeow prove` surface and matching library API that:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:16:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:17:- always loads the complete embedded `gmeow.gts` canon as the immutable base theory, then layers the caller's compact, typed premises and goal onto it without requiring callers to hand-assemble RDF list/formula carriers;
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:18:- lowers that request once into the canonical native `logic:` formula representation and runs the native prover;
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:19:- can emit the exact TPTP-FOF problem for external proof tooling, reusing #1751 rather than creating a second exporter;
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:20:- returns a stable machine-readable verdict with proof/evidence references, standpoint, provenance, loss evidence, and the logical stage contract;
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:21:- detects ordinary domain triples that appear intended as proof premises but lack a certified correspondence/lowering, and fails with an actionable diagnostic instead of silently ignoring them;
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:22:- uses registered typed correspondence laws when domain vocabulary is admitted into logic, without treating bounded-corpus success as authority for unrestricted rewrites.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:23:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:24:## Acceptance criteria
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:25:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:26:- `gmeow prove REQUEST` works from the installed consumer binary and always reasons against the complete embedded GMEOW bundle; there is no module-selection path that can silently omit canon axioms.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:27:- Every verdict records the exact embedded bundle identity and preserves evidence/provenance links into that canon.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:28:- A documented minimal request can express the navigation obligation from #1755 and receives the expected rejection/proof result.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:29:- The equivalent canonical carrier request yields the same verdict and evidence.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:30:- An unlowered domain-triple version fails explicitly and explains how to supply or select the required correspondence; it cannot produce a misleading success.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:31:- Native execution and TPTP export share the same lowered request and symbol table, with no serialize/reparse round trip.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:32:- Output supports a deterministic JSON form suitable for applications, plus concise human output.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:33:- Product tests cover GMEOW request lowering, verdicts, diagnostics, and evidence. They do not duplicate PurRDF RDF/SPARQL/GTS conformance tests.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:34:- Documentation includes one copy-paste CLI example and one library example.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:35:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:36:## Relationships
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:37:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:38:- Consumer report and carrier-visibility bug: #1755
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:39:- TPTP-FOF exporter and external prover harness: #1751
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:40:- Correspondence-calculus production work: #1712, #1737, #1738
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:41:- Parent implementation plan: #1704
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:42:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:43:Principles 4, 7, 12, 17, 18, and 19 apply.
