.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:48:### paudley — 2026-09-17T21:38:10Z
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:49:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:50:Critical distribution requirement: `gmeow` MUST be one self-contained executable containing the prover CLI, the complete authenticated `gmeow.gts` theory, the GMN codebook, and every runtime asset required by `gmeow prove`. Consumers and proof guards MUST NOT depend on an adjacent data directory, an older checkout, `target/`, or the removed `fol-tptp-export` path. The supported build/install workflow must materialize and authenticate the producer outputs first, then build and stage this single consumer executable at `dist/bin/gmeow`; invoking it from any working directory must provide the whole GMEOW theory. Add acceptance coverage that removes/withholds the source checkout and generated tree before executing a proof with the staged binary.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:51:
