.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:56:Already present on `main`:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:57:- the public `gmeow prove` command and bounded E/Vampire protocol;
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:58:- an embedded `gmeow.gts` and embedded GMN codebook;
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:59:- protocol-focused prover tests and a blinded-working-directory bundle test;
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:60:- source-first `make install`, which produces `dist/bin/gmeow`.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:61:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:62:Confirmed gaps:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:63:1. `prove` currently compiles only caller-supplied RDF. It never loads the embedded canon, so the executable contains the theory but the proof operation does not use it.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:64:2. `make cli-build` is documented as the consumer build entry point but merely depends on `producer-build`; a clean tree still lacks the bundle/codebook. `make install` works only because it performs sync beforehand.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:65:3. The bundle has a guarded build-time path; the GMN codebook is embedded through an unguarded source-tree-relative path.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:66:4. Existing self-sufficiency coverage exercises `info` and `transpile`, not the staged `dist/bin/gmeow prove` path.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:67:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:68:Implementation slice:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:69:- compose the authenticated embedded canon with caller inputs in memory before the single logic lowering, and record the exact bundle identity in the proof receipt;
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:70:- guard and override both embedded asset paths in `build.rs`, while retaining one executable and no runtime asset directory;
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:71:- split the internal already-materialized consumer build from the public source-first `cli-build` target so `install` still invokes the producer exactly once;
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:72:- add a staged-binary proof acceptance from a blinded cwd with an empty environment and an absolute stub-prover path, proving the executable requires no checkout/generated directory at runtime;
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:73:- update consumer docs and Make contract tests.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:74:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:75:The existing typed-request/native-prover and ungrounded-domain-triple diagnostics in the issue remain broader semantic work unless they are already exposed by the current lowering. This slice fixes the critical distribution failure and the discovered canon-omission bug without creating a second proof implementation. Principles 4, 7, 12, 17, 18, and 19 govern the change.
