.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:79:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:80:The complete-canon experiment found a real semantic blocker rather than a packaging failure. Current canon admission yields 327 explicit FOF blockers (266 class-expression, 51 standpoint/modal context, seven Contract-owner, two binding-guard, one probabilistic-profile). I recorded the exact remediation and producer-precompiled-base requirement in #1770.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:81:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1768-next-prover-current.txt:82:This implementation will therefore ship the urgent one-file distribution contract without silently discarding those units: source-first build/install, guarded embedded bundle + codebook, signed release-bundle embedding, and a staged-binary smoke that makes the checkout inaccessible while `prove` and GMN execute. #1770 blocks the broader full-canon proof semantics in this issue.
