.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:42:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:43:Current source audit for the historical probability-model blocker:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:44:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:45:The authored logic module already declares `FullIndependence` as a
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:46:`ProbabilityModel`. The compiler's structural admission recognizes a declared
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:47:model under both RDF typing and native `logic:instanceOf`; it only consults the
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:48:selected default graph. This does not select an independence model for an actual
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:49:probabilistic query, which still requires its explicit model declaration.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:50:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:51:The combined candidate strengthens the existing compiler regression to cover both
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:52:typing surfaces, require the emitted contract, and retain its uncertainty facet.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:53:A new synthetic named-graph control requires the hard contract diagnostic when
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:54:the only model is outside the selected graph. Together with the existing absent-
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:55:model and native structural-typing controls, the selection passed 4/4. Source lint
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:56:and producer-independent strict Clippy also passed.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:57:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:58:These test-only changes do not establish a new full-canon blocker count. The
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:59:historical 327-unit inventory belongs to its original bundle/selection and must
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:60:be remeasured on the authenticated new product; it is not a reason to invent a
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:61:model or erase graph context. The complete prepared-canon, request composition,
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:62:grounding-diagnostic, native/external proof and blinded consumer requirements
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:63:remain open. Current production CLI routing still compiles caller files, so the
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:64:one-file distribution evidence alone cannot establish those requirements.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:65:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:66:The existing optimized producer build continues for the authenticated bootstrap.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:67:No new PR is being opened, and no full proof or issue completion is claimed.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/issue1770-next-proof-current.txt:68:
