thub.com/actions/upload-artifact/commit/c2acdedd35a8824a1552c7137f8c18288c3ea469\"><code>c2acded</code></a> chore: prepare v7.0.2 release</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/actions/upload-artifact/commit/4687c1bbaa0a58abb517d90b4bbade6754c80c1a\"><code>4687c1b</code></a> Merge pull request <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/upload-artifact/issues/821\">#821</a> from actions/tunc-d-upload-artifact-package-bump</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/actions/upload-artifact/commit/8cbe1bebdb858105d8fdd88f81404d4de4595719\"><code>8cbe1be</code></a> Bump <code>@​actions/artifact</code> to 6.3.1</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a href=\"https://github.com/actions/upload-artifact/compare/043fb46d1a93c77aae656e7c1c64a875d1fc6a0a...cf430e030ddbb5b0abf93d22962f4752f3646cd9\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility score](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=actions/upload-artifact&package-manager=github_actions&previous-version=7.0.1&new-version=7.0.2)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't alter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting `@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits that have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n\n\n</details>","headRefName":"dependabot/github_actions/actions/upload-artifact-7.0.2","number":1821,"title":"chore(deps): bump actions/upload-artifact from 7.0.1 to 7.0.2","url":"https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-ontology/pull/1821"},{"baseRefName":"main","body":"Bumps [actions/setup-node](https://github.com/actions/setup-node) from 7.0.0 to 7.1.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/actions/setup-node/releases\">actions/setup-node's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v7.1.0</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<h3>Enhancements:</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add support for mise.toml file by <a href=\"https://github.com/gperdomor\"><code>@​gperdomor</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1421\">actions/setup-node#1421</a></li>\n<li>Support absolute paths in node-version-file by <a href=\"https://github.com/v-mahabaleshwars\"><code>@​v-mahabaleshwars</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1633\">actions/setup-node#1633</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug fixes:</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add Node version validation and manifest fetch retry by <a href=\"https://github.com/v-jitenderpalsingh\"><code>@​v-jitenderpalsingh</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1580\">actions/setup-node#1580</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation updates:</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>README.md: bump actions/checkout to latest version 7 by <a href=\"https://github.com/deining\"><code>@​deining</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1578\">actions/setup-node#1578</a></li>\n<li>docs: add V7 ESM migration and NODE_AUTH_TOKEN behavior change by <a href=\"https://github.com/v-gowridurgad\"><code>@​v-gowridurgad</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1593\">actions/setup-node#1593</a></li>\n<li>Fixed cache recommendation syntax by <a href=\"https://github.com/SubJunk\"><code>@​SubJunk</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1603\">actions/setup-node#1603</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Dependency updates:</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Update workflow pins and migrate Node matrices to modern versions by <a href=\"https://github.com/v-HarithaVattikuti\"><code>@​v-HarithaVattikuti</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1583\">actions/setup-node#1583</a></li>\n<li>Upgrade  <code>@​actions/cache</code> to 6.2.0 by <a href=\"https://github.com/philip-gai\"><code>@​philip-gai</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1584\">actions/setup-node#1584</a></li>\n<li>Pin <code>@​types/node</code> to v24 by <a href=\"https://github.com/v-priyagupta108\"><code>@​v-priyagupta108</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1585\">actions/setup-node#1585</a></li>\n<li>Override brace-expansion to 5.0.8 by <a href=\"https://github.com/v-priyagupta108\"><code>@​v-priyagupta108</code></a> with <a href=\"https://github.com/Copilot\"><code>@​Copilot</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1599\">actions/setup-node#1599</a></li>\n<li>Upgrade  actions/checkout from 7.0.0 to 7.0.1 by <a href=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1598\">actions/setup-node#1598</a></li>\n<li>Upgrade  prettier from 3.8.4 to 3.9.6 by <a href=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1590\">actions/setup-node#1590</a></li>\n<li>Upgrade  <code>@​vercel/ncc</code> from 0.44.0 to 0.45.0 by <a href=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1610\">actions/setup-node#1610</a></li>\n<li>Upgrade  pnpm/action-setup from 6.0.9 to 6.0.10 by <a href=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1602\">actions/setup-node#1602</a></li>\n<li>Upgrade  baseline-browser-mapping from 2.10.38 to 2.11.22 by <a href=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1629\">actions/setup-node#1629</a></li>\n<li>Upgrade <code>@​types/semver</code> from 7.7.1 to 7.8.0 by <a href=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1616\">actions/setup-node#1616</a></li>\n<li>Upgrade <code>@​typescript-eslint/parser</code> from 8.62.0 to 8.70.0 by <a href=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1615\">actions/setup-node#1615</a></li>\n<li>Upgrade pnpm/action-setup from 6.0.10 to 6.1.0 by <a href=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1631\">actions/setup-node#1631</a></li>\n<li>Upgrade jest-each from 30.4.1 to 30.5.2 by <a href=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1636\">actions/setup-node#1636</a></li>\n<li>Upgrade eslint-plugin-n from 18.1.0 to 18.3.0 by <a href=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1638\">actions/setup-node#1638</a></li>\n<li>Update dependencies and add license files by <a href=\"https://github.com/v-HarithaVattikuti\"><code>@​v-HarithaVattikuti</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1642\">actions/setup-node#1642</a></li>\n<li>Upgrade eslint from 10.5.0 to 10.11.0 and package.json from 7.0.0 to 7.1.0 by <a href=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1635\">actions/setup-node#1635</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/v-jitenderpalsingh\"><code>@​v-jitenderpalsingh</code></a> made their first contribution in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1580\">actions/setup-node#1580</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/philip-gai\"><code>@​philip-gai</code></a> made their first contribution in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1584\">actions/setup-node#1584</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/gperdomor\"><code>@​gperdomor</code></a> made their first contribution in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1421\">actions/setup-node#1421</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/SubJunk\"><code>@​SubJunk</code></a> made their first contribution in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/pull/1603\">actions/setup-node#1603</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/actions/setup-node/compare/v7.0.0...v7.1.0\">https://github.com/actions/setup-node/compare/v7.0.0...v7.1.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/actions/setup-node/commit/949feb2413d6458794dcd2491c4babbbce0c15c1\"><code>949feb2</code></a> Bump eslint from 10.5.0 to 10.11.0 and package.json from 7.0.0 to 7.1.0 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/issues/1635\">#1635</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/actions/setup-node/commit/7207c4f1189c7ee83ddf20c7c68bd1af6fdd751c\"><code>7207c4f</code></a> chore: update dependencies and add license files (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/issues/1642\">#1642</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/actions/setup-node/commit/54337e0d02de9202d0948aaff36ad556375497b9\"><code>54337e0</code></a> Bump eslint-plugin-n from 18.1.0 to 18.3.0 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/issues/1638\">#1638</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/actions/setup-node/commit/fb54fa8c14c63410cc752f0ae3b7b3ca6af161fc\"><code>fb54fa8</code></a> Bump jest-each from 30.4.1 to 30.5.2 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/issues/1636\">#1636</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/actions/setup-node/commit/7f84f1d52d0c56afb45c62fee31a93b843cea4d6\"><code>7f84f1d</code></a> Bump pnpm/action-setup from 6.0.10 to 6.1.0 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/issues/1631\">#1631</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/actions/setup-node/commit/0c54c7b07420dcba69a7d832587f55ebdf771c9e\"><code>0c54c7b</code></a> Bump <code>@​typescript-eslint/parser</code> from 8.62.0 to 8.70.0 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/issues/1615\">#1615</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/actions/setup-node/commit/a8294190049a9c296f01b9a432aff41dd83d8284\"><code>a829419</code></a> Bump <code>@​types/semver</code> from 7.7.1 to 7.8.0 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/issues/1616\">#1616</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/actions/setup-node/commit/680d1e489b82f1243de15bc7665c0007e3c9a860\"><code>680d1e4</code></a> Support absolute paths in node-version-file (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/issues/1633\">#1633</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/actions/setup-node/commit/db0fb3a98ed314b69026b6e8c9be26a7e2fe65a8\"><code>db0fb3a</code></a> Bump baseline-browser-mapping from 2.10.38 to 2.11.22 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/issues/1629\">#1629</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/actions/setup-node/commit/94196ee1d15439c1b6651cd87ef14e88ec435966\"><code>94196ee</code></a> Bump pnpm/action-setup from 6.0.9 to 6.0.10 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-node/issues/1602\">#1602</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/actions/setup-node/compare/820762786026740c76f36085b0efc47a31fe5020...949feb2413d6458794dcd2491c4babbbce0c15c1\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility score](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=actions/setup-node&package-manager=github_actions&previous-version=7.0.0&new-version=7.1.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't alter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting `@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits that have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n\n\n</details>","headRefName":"dependabot/github_actions/actions/setup-node-7.1.0","number":1820,"title":"chore(deps): bump actions/setup-node from 7.0.0 to 7.1.0","url":"https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-ontology/pull/1820"},{"baseRefName":"main","body":"Bumps [dorny/test-reporter](https://github.com/dorny/test-reporter) from 3.0.0 to 3.2.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/dorny/test-reporter/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">dorny/test-reporter's changelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>Changelog</h1>\n<h2>3.2.0</h2>\n<h3>Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix: <code>dotnet-trx</code> reports unmapped test outcomes and aborted test runs as failures <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/pull/825\">dorny/test-reporter#825</a></li>\n<li>Fix: report test cases from nested <!-- raw HTML omitted --> elements in <code>java-junit</code> reporter <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/pull/840\">dorny/test-reporter#840</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>3.1.0</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add <code>list-files</code> input to control test report file listing <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/pull/773\">dorny/test-reporter#773</a></li>\n<li>Add <code>summary_file</code> output with the path to the generated summary in Markdown format <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/pull/772\">dorny/test-reporter#772</a></li>\n<li>Add Unreal Engine JSON reporter support.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Preserve PHPUnit exception types when the failure body does not contain a typed line.</li>\n<li>Parse Jest JUnit failures that provide failure attributes without a failure body.</li>\n<li>Escape pipe characters in Markdown table cells.</li>\n<li>Decode report files before parsing and handle byte-order marks correctly.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Maintenance and security</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Update dependencies and rebuild the distribution to include security fixes and current tooling.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>3.0.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Feature: Use NodeJS 24 LTS as default runtime <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/pull/738\">dorny/test-reporter#738</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.7.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Feature: Add <code>slug-prefix</code> output for link anchors <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/pull/731\">dorny/test-reporter#731</a></li>\n<li>Feature: Report <code>jest-junit</code> testsuite errors as failures <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/pull/155\">dorny/test-reporter#155</a></li>\n<li>Security: Update dependencies to fix reported security vulnerabilities</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.6.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix: For <code>workflow_run</code> events, resolve the commit of the check run from related pull request head commits first (matching <code>workflow_run.head_branch</code>, then first PR), and fall back to <code>workflow_run.head_sha</code> for non-PR runs <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/pull/673\">dorny/test-reporter#673</a></li>\n<li>Change: The <code>test-reporter</code> action will listed all artifacts associated with the build run <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/pull/693\">dorny/test-reporter#693</a></li>\n<li>Maintenance: Upgrade to ESLint v9 <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/pull/629\">dorny/test-reporter#629</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.5.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Feature: Add Nette Tester support with <code>tester-junit</code> reporter <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/pull/707\">dorny/test-reporter#707</a></li>\n<li>Maintenance: Bump actions/upload-artifact from 5 to 6 <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/pull/695\">dorny/test-reporter#695</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.4.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Feature: Add PHPUnit support with JUnit XML dialect parser <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/pull/422\">dorny/test-reporter#422</a></li>\n<li>Feature: Add JUnit XML sample files and tests for validation <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/pull/701\">dorny/test-reporter#701</a></li>\n<li>Fix: Refactor deprecated <code>String.substr()</code> function to use <code>String.substring()</code> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/pull/704\">dorny/test-reporter#704</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.3.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Feature: Add Python support with <code>python-xunit</code> reporter (pytest) <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/pull/643\">dorny/test-reporter#643</a></li>\n<li>Feature: Add pytest traceback parsing and <code>directory-mapping</code> option <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/pull/238\">dorny/test-reporter#238</a></li>\n<li>Performance: Update sax.js to fix large XML file parsing <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/pull/681\">dorny/test-reporter#681</a></li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/dorny/test-reporter/commit/d1b5dff021aa968b288b02285a8bf47471c5928a\"><code>d1b5dff</code></a> test-reporter release v3.2.0</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/dorny/test-reporter/commit/aa2d703c08ef79f4a13b6b944885e757cc2bd687\"><code>aa2d703</code></a> Merge pull request <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/issues/840\">#840</a> from keith-lueneburg/fix/junit-nested-testsuites</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/dorny/test-reporter/commit/be1e6af3b6f0247ca8523d52c4fa56c21fd907b3\"><code>be1e6af</code></a> Merge pull request <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/issues/842\">#842</a> from dorny/dependabot/npm_and_yarn/reports/jest/multi...</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/dorny/test-reporter/commit/79718dcaaae3b6e11f621a35ac9a127a4c0256d2\"><code>79718dc</code></a> Merge pull request <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/issues/825\">#825</a> from CTWalk/fix/dotnet-trx-unmapped-outcomes</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/dorny/test-reporter/commit/98640f9fdf91478704a357b87dfdf292d624c7eb\"><code>98640f9</code></a> fix(dotnet-trx): treat a Warning run outcome as a clean run</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/dorny/test-reporter/commit/186413b9aad57244ef29ed807432d8d821af062b\"><code>186413b</code></a> fix(dotnet-trx): report unmapped outcomes and aborted runs as failures</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/dorny/test-reporter/commit/c5f7127dc95ed3cba6cc223314416a5a50dc23f1\"><code>c5f7127</code></a> chore(deps): bump brace-expansion in /reports/jest</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/dorny/test-reporter/commit/53f83686b9756940da8bb936cea68050c38f1026\"><code>53f8368</code></a> Merge pull request <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/dorny/test-reporter/issues/841\">#841</a> from dorny/dependabot/npm_and_yarn/typescript-eslint/...</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/dorny/test-reporter/commit/edc93d264fc36765b2d24974cca43b6dc66cd023\"><code>edc93d2</code></a> chore(deps-dev): bump <code>@​typescript-eslint/parser</code> from 8.70.1 to 8.71.0</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/dorny/test-reporter/commit/1896380dca5565b7f5bbe81238b8716dc2a49bc4\"><code>1896380</code></a> Rebuild the <code>dist/index.js</code> file</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/dorny/test-reporter/compare/a43b3a5f7366b97d083190328d2c652e1a8b6aa2...d1b5dff021aa968b288b02285a8bf47471c5928a\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility score](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=dorny/test-reporter&package-manager=github_actions&previous-version=3.0.0&new-version=3.2.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't alter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting `@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits that have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n\n\n</details>","headRefName":"dependabot/github_actions/dorny/test-reporter-3.2.0","number":1819,"title":"chore(deps): bump dorny/test-reporter from 3.0.0 to 3.2.0","url":"https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-ontology/pull/1819"},{"baseRefName":"main","body":"Found while making native reasoning run on the production corpus (#1757, PR #1802). The production `rl-default` world was **genuinely inconsistent**: the native reasoner proved 11 records to be `logic:Nothing`, and purrdf's OWL-Direct consistency check agrees. There were two authoring errors.\n\n## 1. `logic:message` values tagged against a plain-string range\n- `logic:message` declares `rdfs:range xsd:string`, and 480 of its 497 values are plain strings. **17 carried `@x-gmeow-english`.** That makes them `rdf:langString`, which OWL 2 and RDF 1.1 make disjoint from `xsd:string`, so each record was unsatisfiable.\n- Ten production records were proved `logic:Nothing` by two independent rules (`dl:datatype-membership-clash` and `refute:datatype-value-space`).\n- **Fix:** untag the 17 outliers (10 in the logic slice, 7 slice-manifest constraints in `vocabulary.ttl`), keeping the precise range. That was chosen explicitly over widening or retyping the range.\n- None of the 17 is an advice carrier bound verbatim to tagged source prose, and none was extracted into an i18n `.po` catalogue.\n\n## 2. Thing-qualified counts on datatype properties\n- 22 qualified cardinality restrictions on **datatype** properties named `logic:onClass logic:Thing`. OWL 2 keeps the object and data domains disjoint, so no literal can meet a Thing qualifier:\n  - **`minQualifiedCardinality`** made every instance of its class **unsatisfiable**. The chase minted a resource witness for `lang:unicodeNormalization` and proved `gmeow:gatePolicyProse` `logic:Nothing` (`dl:datatype-property-literal-clash`).\n  - **`maxQualifiedCardinality`** was **vacuous**: it counted Thing-valued successors a datatype property never has, so the intended at-most bound went unenforced.\n- **Fix:** all 22 now qualify by `logic:onDataRange rdfs:Literal`, the form two existing restrictions already use. They span affect, agentic, calendar, gts, norms, images, lang and math.\n- A corpus scan (872 datatype properties, both declaration layouts) finds none left.\n\n## Checks\n- Every changed file parses.\n- The pre-commit hooks pass.","headRefName":"fix-logic-message-untag","number":1804,"title":"fix(slices): repair the corpus inconsistencies native reasoning exposed","url":"https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-ontology/pull/1804"},{"baseRefName":"main","body":"Part of #1757 and #1796. The branch contains the prerequisite work from #1793, #1798, #1799, #1800 and #1801, plus the corpus repairs from #1804. These dependencies need individual acceptance and sequential ghprsq integration.\n\nThe production reasoner previously refused or stalled while constructing its input-specific termination certificate. This change specializes settled schema joins without combinatorial products, keeps typed statement positions separate from variable-predicate encodings, computes joint acyclicity by Horn propagation, and adds Datalog-first restricted scheduling and restricted joint acyclicity. Cardinality clashes are evaluated once per class with world-local evidence. Diagnostics retain withheld reads and name obstruction/cost owners.\n\nThe current review repair preserves clause exactness and ordinary distinct guards through lowering and specialization. Restricted blocking reads exact native premises separately from the coarser vocabulary quotient, so it cannot fabricate an inverse by identifying ordinary data URIs. Relaxed clauses, lossy pair bridges and unknown-count witness summaries cannot supply guaranteed blocking evidence. Valid mixed operator spellings remain certifiable. anyURI facets and enumeration equality use PurRDF's XML whitespace normalizer; finite-write bounds saturate. The native artifact fixture repair from #1782 retains real execution evidence and checks missing/mismatched receipts. Unused csv/flate2 dependencies and the reported lint defects are removed.\n\nPublished development units through 1d5d7f36d: fixture repair 13a44f7a9, restricted blocking d3ca06032, anyURI equality 551dee071 and dependency cleanup 1d5d7f36d. Verification on the combined working source:\n\n- make fmt passed.\n- Focused synthetic nextest passed 152 tests (3801 skipped), including the formerly false certificate, variable-count witness summaries, positive grounded inverses, native artifact fixtures, datatype plans and actual generated numeric-range validation. Nextest d240e531-3bac-4fe6-b5bb-3141da4549f5.\n- make lint passed.\n- Normal commit and push succeeded without bypass.\n\nThe numeric math range/compiler repair is still uncommitted pending full qualification; its focused consumer controls passed, and its review finding remains open. Two authenticated artifact-verifier cases are preserved and have not passed yet. The focused runner correctly refuses absent producer-selected law fixtures.\n\nAcceptance is still open. The full gate, authenticated fixture production, production verdict and two independent cold generations/output comparison have not passed on this head. The last hosted fixture-prefix run failed at stage-docs-render with an unsupported reasoning verdict. Earlier production execution published a reasoning receipt and 692,948 inferred axioms; that is historical execution evidence, not a completed gate on the current commit.\n\nThe remaining class-model work follows #1803's ownership agreement: PurRDF owns generic DL/chase engines; GMEOW owns logic semantics and world-scoped provenance. The historical released-3.0.0 benchmark does not decide the two large worlds within its selected budget. The three datatype/property-chain boundary issues are now merged upstream, beyond the latest published 3.0.1 release; current GMEOW locks still select 3.0.0. GMEOW's rule-reification defect #1805 is in active implementation on an isolated branch. Capability, production and full-gate work remain acceptance requirements.\n\nCurrent CodeRabbit findings require reassessment against the new head. No independent completion audit or merge readiness is claimed. Principles 4, 7, 12, 15, 17, 18 and 19.\n","headRefName":"issue-1757-production-verdict","number":1802,"title":"fix(1757): certify and run native reasoning on the production corpus","url":"https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-ontology/pull/1802"},{"baseRefName":"main","body":"Part of #1757. This targets `main` directly and is independent of the RJA stack.\n\n**Problem:** joint acyclicity was cubic in program size.\n- For every existential, `move_set` re-scanned every flow until nothing changed.\n- Each `move_contains` call scanned the whole position universe twice.\n- The edge loop rescanned all existentials for every edge and recomputed refined positions on every check.\n\nMeasured on a synthetic program: doubling the size made it 8.4× slower (1.6 s → 13.4 s). A 25k-rule statement program would take hours. The input-specific certifier reaches JA once #1796 lets witness families leave the weak-acyclicity-only path, which is how this surfaced.\n\n**Fix:**\n- A move set Ω_v is a Horn least fixpoint: a flow fires when *all* its body positions are covered. So each move set is now one **Dowling–Gallier counter propagation** (1984) over a `MoveIndex` built once, linear in program size.\n- The conservative sibling rule (a slot with both wildcard and constant refinements) is precomputed per slot. The first time a slot is occupied, all of its body positions are covered at once.\n- Consumer frontier positions and rule→existential owners are indexed once, in `JointGraph`.\n- Acyclicity is a single **Kahn** elimination. `node_reaches_self` stays for SWA, which checks only a subset of nodes.\n\n**Equivalence:** a 5,000-program differential run against the previous implementation, scratch only and not committed, matched every verdict and every evidence string, edge counts included. The programs were random and mixed wildcard and constant refinements, inverses and cycles: 3,486 certified and 1,514 refused.\n\n**Speed:** with 200 existential rules and 2,000 Datalog rules, the check drops from 13.4 s to 6 ms. With 2,000 and 20,000 it takes 177 ms.\n\n**Regression:** the gmeow-logic failure set matches main exactly (167, the same set). Clippy reports nothing new on changed lines.","headRefName":"issue-1757-ja-linear","number":1801,"title":"perf(1757): compute joint acyclicity in linear Horn propagation","url":"https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-ontology/pull/1801"},{"baseRefName":"issue-1757-snapshot-critical","body":"Fixes #1795. Stacked on #1793.\n\nThe input-specific termination certificate was refusing production because of encoding coarseness, not real cycles. Two commits:\n\n**`7a285ccfb`: per-atom encoding, fresh-null keys, count-1 minimums**\n- **P2:** the global `fixed_relations` switch is gone.\n  - Constant-predicate atoms keep binary, class-refined positions. Only variable-predicate atoms go to the pair relations.\n  - Weak acyclicity links the two encodings only along subject/object flows with matching class keys.\n  - JA, SWA and MSA get non-existential Datalog bridge rules between the encodings.\n- **P3:** a head position whose partner is a fresh existential gets the key `Null`, which feeds only wildcard reads. Stored nulls are never rewritten: sameAs only derives, refutations only write `instanceOf Nothing`, and DL blocking reuses an older witness.\n- **P4:** a minimum family with count 1 is analysed with one witness and no `differentFrom`. The count stays in the deduplication key. Such a family still goes through WA only: letting it use the other rungs made an existing test use more than 24 GB.\n\n**`4e7c7f2a7`: closed witness-free relations (P1)**\n- A predicate, or a (predicate, constant object) pair, counts as closed when every producer that can write it creates no witnesses and reads only immutable or closed relations. Membership is decided by dropping candidates until stable.\n- The closure is a semi-naive Datalog fixpoint over the source rows and feeds specialization. The induction proof is in the `Closure` doc comment.\n- If the closure exceeds the 2^18 bound, the certificate falls back to immutable relations only, and the refusal names the reason.\n- When the first pass certifies, the 1,383 s second pass is skipped.\n\n**Tests and mutation checks:**\n- 7 chase tests, 6 input tests and 4 admission tests.\n- Disabling each mechanism fails at least one test.\n- With the writer check disabled, all three refusal tests wrongly certify.\n- These cases stay refused, as intended:\n  - `p range R` with `R ⊑ ≥1 p`;\n  - a subclass path back into the restriction;\n  - the finance inverse pair, which is handled in #1796 (#1798 and #1799).\n\n**Regression:**\n- gmeow-logic: the 167 failures are the same set as the baseline.\n- `stages::reason`: the same 3 failures as on unmodified code.\n- Clippy reports nothing new on changed lines.\n\n**Not yet verified:** the effect on the production refusal (11,202 violations), pending a combined production run.","headRefName":"issue-1795-certifier-encoding","number":1800,"title":"fix(1795): sharpen termination-statement encoding and bind closed relations","url":"https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-ontology/pull/1800"},{"baseRefName":"issue-1796-datalog-first","body":"Part 2 of #1796, stacked on #1798 (Datalog-first schedule).\n\nAdds the **restricted joint acyclicity** (RJA) rung to the termination certificate ladder (Carral, Dragoste & Krötzsch 2017, Def. 4). An edge v→w of the JA dependency graph is dropped when the Datalog closure of the frozen consumer body, the producer head and the producer body already satisfies the consumer head. Genuine inverse-pair existential cycles (`p ⊑ ∃r`, `r⁻` back-edge) therefore certify and run **without a budget**.\n\n- Sound only for the Datalog-first restricted chase (#1798).\n- Runs as the **last** rung, so programs already certified by WA/JA/SWA/MSA keep their class. Rank: RJA=5.\n- Poset meets: RJA∧SWA=WA, RJA∧MSA=JA.\n- Only exact Datalog rules feed the blocking closure. Any rule with a numeric guard, `distinct`, negation or witness minting is excluded, so guarded rules never block a trigger.\n- The LOGIC-PERFORMANCE.md ladder doctrine names the rung.\n\nTests: `chase.tests.rs` (certifies the inverse pair; refuses without the inverse; meets with incomparable classes; a guarded rule doesn't block) and `list_tests.rs` (the inverse pair runs unbudgeted with one witness).\n\nMutation checks:\n- Never blocking fails the certify and unbudgeted tests.\n- Dropping the `distinct` exclusion fails the guard test.\n\nThe gmeow-logic regression matches the main baseline exactly: 2054 passed, 167 failed, and the failures are the same set as on main.\n\nUpstream lift to purrdf is tracked in #1797.","headRefName":"issue-1796-rja","number":1799,"title":"feat(1796): certify restricted joint acyclicity","url":"https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-ontology/pull/1799"},{"baseRefName":"main","body":"Part 1 of #1796, the precondition for the restricted-chase termination certificate.\n\n## Problem\nThe joint materializer gathered every producer against one frozen round snapshot (*\"Every producer reads the same cross-world frozen round\"*). So an existential trigger was checked **before** the Datalog consequences of earlier witnesses existed. For example, with `JournalEntry ⊑ ≥2 journalEntryPostings.Posting`, an inverse property, and `Posting ⊑ ∃postingJournalEntry.JournalEntry`:\n- the posting's back edge to its entry was derived in the same round in which the reverse restriction was checked;\n- so a fresh entry was minted every round, and the chase never terminated, even though the authored axioms are satisfiable with one witness.\n\n## Change (`crates/logic/src/physical/seminaive/joint.rs`)\n- **Datalog-first rounds.** Within each stratum, witness-minting producers (existential rules and generative witness families, gmeow's only witness mint sites) fire only in a round that follows a Datalog-only round with nothing left to add.\n- **No lost triggers.** Witness producers read every row committed since they last gathered: a per-world generative row span plus accumulated changed predicates. Semi-naive evaluation therefore loses no trigger across the Datalog-only rounds they sit out.\n- **Completion order.** A stratum concludes blocked or complete only after its witness producers have had their round.\n- **Same guarantees.** It stays deterministic (sorted commit unchanged) and mints a subset of the interleaved schedule's witnesses.\n- **Doctrine.** `slices/grounding/logic/design/LOGIC-PERFORMANCE.md` records the rule in its chase doctrine.\n\n## Tests\n- `an_inverse_back_edge_satisfies_the_reverse_restriction_under_datalog_first`: the inverse-pair program closes with **one** witness and the derived back edge. With Datalog-first disabled it **exhausts** its budget, verified by mutation.\n- Two regressions caught by existing tests during development are fixed:\n  - Blocked strata must still give witness producers their round (`empty_nominal_guard_remains_in_joint_invention_admission`).\n  - The generative round must re-evaluate the Datalog producers' last span, so value-interpretation withholding is not lost (`functional_property_distinct_xml_literals_are_withheld`, `unknown_value_interpretations_withhold_only_the_affected_law`).\n\n## Verification\n- `cargo nextest run -p gmeow-logic`: 2215 run, 167 failed. The failure set is **identical** to `main`'s; all 167 need producer fixtures.\n- `cargo nextest run -p gmeow-pipeline -E 'test(/stages::reason|witness|chase/)'`: 16/23 pass. The 7 failures all need `GMEOW_TEST_FIXTURE_MANIFEST` or the bundle-import cache.\n- Clippy reports no hits on changed lines.\n\n## Next\nPart 2 adds the **restricted joint acyclicity** rung (sound under this schedule) so such programs are *certified* and run without a budget. Generated outputs may change when the producer next runs, because fewer witnesses are minted.","headRefName":"issue-1796-datalog-first","number":1798,"title":"feat(1796): run the restricted chase Datalog-first","url":"https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-ontology/pull/1798"},{"baseRefName":"main","body":"Closes #1790.\n\n## Problem\n`publish` (`crates/logic/src/reason/program.rs`) copied the single joint execution admission into every world's `ChaseCertificate`. So the three termination-ladder demonstrator worlds all published the joint class:\n- the shipped bundle could not carry their `chase.certificate.{jointly,super-weakly,model-summarizing}-acyclic` findings, which `crates/pipeline/tests/chase_certificate_golden.rs` expects;\n- the demonstrator docs' claim that `stage-reason` hard-fails on a wrong class was false.\n\n## Changes\n- **`reason/program.rs`:** `execute` groups the prepared source existential rules by world and passes them to `publish`. A world with authored rules publishes `ChaseAdmission::certify(own rules)` when that certifies; every other world keeps the joint admission that authorized execution. No certificate claims more than was proved.\n- **`termination_demonstrators.rs`:** `termination_ladder_certificate_codes()` declares each demonstrator world's required finding code, next to the existing registry.\n- **`pipeline/stages/reason.rs`:** `require_demonstrator_classes` refuses the stage when a present demonstrator world publishes any other class. The producer always roots the demonstrators into the object-level EDB, and the golden test requires their findings in the shipped bundle.\n\n## Tests\n- `each_demonstrator_world_publishes_its_own_certificate_class` (gmeow-logic): the demonstrators, rooted as the producer roots them, are reasoned by `reason_all`, and each world publishes its declared class. It fails if `publish` copies the joint admission again.\n- `demonstrator_worlds_must_publish_their_declared_certificate_class` (gmeow-pipeline):\n  - the declared classes pass;\n  - a copied weakly-acyclic admission is refused;\n  - an input without demonstrator worlds passes.\n\n## Verification\n- `cargo nextest run -p gmeow-logic`: 2216 run, 167 failed. That set is **identical** to `main`'s; all 167 need producer fixtures.\n- `cargo nextest run -p gmeow-pipeline -E 'test(/stages::reason/)'`: 12/15 pass. The 3 failures need `GMEOW_TEST_FIXTURE_MANIFEST`.\n  - A first version also refused inputs without demonstrator worlds and broke 8 synthetic stage-reason tests; enforcement now applies only to present worlds.\n- Clippy reports no hits on changed lines.\n- Full `make check` is blocked by the pre-existing production termination refusal (#1789, #1793).","headRefName":"issue-1790-demo-certificates","number":1794,"title":"fix(1790): publish each world's own chase certificate and enforce the demonstrator classes","url":"https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-ontology/pull/1794"},{"baseRefName":"main","body":"Refs #1789. A follow-up to #1791: the effective diff against `main` is 6 files.\n\n## Problem\nSince #1791, the input-specific termination certificate runs on the production corpus. But it substituted every immutable join binding into each rule, and production schemas multiply out: it exhausted its 2^18-statement bound before deciding. In order, it named:\n- `dl:disjointUnion-disjoint`: 45,796 ground pairs from 262,144+ matches;\n- `dl:property-chain`: 88,382 specializations, because list member cells were unlinked to their list.\n\n## Changes (`crates/logic/src/physical/seminaive/joint/input/admission.rs`, `property.rs`, `chase.rs`)\n- **Discharge and project.** A fully bound immutable atom is a ground source row that no termination rung reads, so it is dropped. Join bindings that agree on every still-read variable specialize once.\n- **Ground laws are witnessed once.** When every still-read variable is bound by immutable rows, each specialization is ground: none can carry a null, and all fire on the same predicates. One specialization represents the rule, and the join stops at its first match.\n- **Member cells read their own list.** `analysis_body` left list-member cells unconstrained, so a list operator paired every cell of every list. Property layouts now record each member cell's list head (`analysis_list_cells`, carried on `StatementRule::list_cells`).\n  - When `rdf:first`/`rdf:rest` are proved immutable, the join binds each cell to the cells reachable from that head through `rdf:rest\\*`, shared tails included, before reading it.\n  - Past the analysis bound, cells stay unconstrained: coarser, but every firing is still covered.\n  - Value flow is unchanged.\n- **Honest exhaustion.** The refusal names the exhausting rule with its immutable-match and distinct-specialization counts. If the finer enriched pass cannot complete, the decided first-pass certificate stands, rather than falling back to the source-independent template.\n\n## Tests (admission level; no chase execution)\n- `a_pairwise_list_law_past_the_analysis_bound_is_witnessed_once`: a 600-member disjoint union (360,000 pairs) beside a minimum restriction certifies.\n- `a_list_operator_reads_only_the_cells_of_its_own_list`: a property chain among 600 unrelated two-member lists (1.44M unlinked cell pairs) certifies.\n- Each test fails with exactly its own mechanism disabled.\n\nAn end-to-end version was dropped. A 600-member disjoint union really entails 360,000 `disjointWith` facts, and materializing them OOMs the build slice. #1792 tracks the quadratic class analysis that dominates that run.\n\n## Verification\n- `cargo nextest run -p gmeow-logic`: 2217 run, 167 failed. The failure set is **identical** to `main`'s; all 167 need producer fixtures.\n- Clippy reports no hits on changed lines.\n- Production run in progress. I'll comment with the stage-reason result. Full `make check` cannot pass until production reasoning is admitted; that is the remaining #1789 work, and it is not a regression from this PR.","headRefName":"issue-1757-snapshot-critical","number":1793,"title":"fix(1789): specialize termination analysis without combinatorial products","url":"https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-ontology/pull/1793"}]
