.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1793-consolidation-comments.md:183:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1793-consolidation-comments.md:184:Production result (run 18, this branch merged with current `main`): **the input-specific termination certificate now decides on the full corpus.**
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1793-consolidation-comments.md:185:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1793-consolidation-comments.md:186:- The analysis completed over **22,916 specialized statements**. The `dl:disjointUnion-disjoint` and `dl:property-chain` exhaustions are gone, and the refusal no longer says "not decided".
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1793-consolidation-comments.md:187:- Peak producer RSS was 11.5 GB; stage-reason reached the certificate after about 61 minutes of pipeline time.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1793-consolidation-comments.md:188:- The certificate **refuses** with 11,202 weak-acyclicity cycle edges. These are dominated by generic positions: `differentFrom` objects (1,485), `instanceOf logic:Thing` (614), then `gmeow:Agent` and `gmeow:Entity`. Example: `subject-object[S|<…/skolem/004a4c65…>] -> predicate-object[O|<…/gmeow/skillProficiencyAgent>]`.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1793-consolidation-comments.md:189:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1793-consolidation-comments.md:190:Whether that is a genuine existential cycle in the ontology or an over-approximation (position-only minimum laws force weak acyclicity only; witness `differentFrom` and clash typing may re-enter restricted classes) is under investigation as #1789 follow-up work. This PR stays scoped to the specialization blow-up it fixes.
