.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1798-consolidation-comments.md:46:## Walkthrough
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1798-consolidation-comments.md:47:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1798-consolidation-comments.md:48:The chase and joint executors now defer witness-minting rules until Datalog-only execution makes no progress. The joint executor tracks committed rows and changed predicates between witness gathers. A test covers a Datalog-derived back edge, and the design document describes the scheduling order.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1798-consolidation-comments.md:49:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1798-consolidation-comments.md:50:### Changes
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1798-consolidation-comments.md:51:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1798-consolidation-comments.md:52:**Generative Scheduling**
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1798-consolidation-comments.md:53:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1798-consolidation-comments.md:54:|Layer / File(s)|Summary|
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1798-consolidation-comments.md:55:|:---|:---|
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1798-consolidation-comments.md:56:|**Chase rule classification and scheduling** <br> `crates/logic/src/physical/chase.rs`|Prepared chase rules are classified by whether they mint existential witnesses or reifier nodes. The chase runs Datalog-only rounds first, enables minting rules after a no-progress round, and returns to Datalog-only scheduling after a productive round.|
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1798-consolidation-comments.md:57:|**Joint executor phases and witness gathering** <br> `crates/logic/src/physical/seminaive/joint.rs`|The joint executor schedules generative rounds after eligible empty Datalog rounds. It tracks committed rows and changed predicates between gathers. Witness-frontier properties and minting producers use accumulated changes during generative rounds; other properties and producers continue to use the current round delta.|
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1798-consolidation-comments.md:58:|**Schedule test and design description** <br> `crates/logic/src/reason/program/list_tests.rs`, `slices/grounding/logic/design/LOGIC-PERFORMANCE.md`|The test checks that a Datalog rule derives a back edge for an existentially created posting and that execution creates one witness. The design document describes the schedule and its relation to restricted-chase certificates.|
