.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1799-consolidation-comments.md:54:Integration note: #1800 (#1795) splits the ladder into `certify_ladder(weak, tuples, ladder)`. When this PR and #1800 meet, the RJA rung must read `tuples`, the program closed under #1800's encoding bridges:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1799-consolidation-comments.md:55:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1799-consolidation-comments.md:56:```rust
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1799-consolidation-comments.md:57:.or_else(|| Self::certify_restricted_joint_acyclic(tuples))
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1799-consolidation-comments.md:58:```
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1799-consolidation-comments.md:59:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1799-consolidation-comments.md:60:This is sound because the bridges are plain Datalog rules with no existentials, and RJA already admits such rules into its blocking closure. I verified it in a combined worktree: every new test from both PRs passes, and the only remaining failures are 2 baseline `list_tests` failures.
