te></details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n\n\n<!-- recent_review_end -->\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Summary</summary>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **Bug Fixes**\n  - Joint-acyclicity checks now account for dependencies between related positions when wildcard and constant refinements are mixed, improving certification coverage.\n- **Refactor**\n  - Dependency analysis now uses a shared graph and a streamlined cycle-checking approach instead of repeatedly scanning rules. This changes how checks are performed without adding or removing user-facing capabilities.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Walkthrough\n\nJoint-acyclicity certification now uses a shared `JointGraph` and `MoveIndex` to compute dependency edges. It checks the resulting graph for cycles with Kahn’s algorithm.\n\n### Changes\n\n**Joint-Acyclicity Certification**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|:---|:---|\n|**Graph construction and cycle check** <br> `crates/logic/src/physical/chase.rs`|`JointGraph` precomputes existential moves, consumer frontiers, and rule ownership. `MoveIndex` propagates reachable positions through copied-variable flows and covers sibling positions for ambiguous predicate-slots. `certify_joint_acyclic` uses these results to add dependency edges, then checks for cycles with topological elimination.|\n\n<!-- change_assessment_start -->\n**Priority:** ⬇️ Low\n\n**Estimated code review effort:** 3 (Moderate) | ~25 minutes\n\n<!-- change_assessment_commit:\"92068d6292b81aefe620564ffbbfbb59061b78b1\" -->\n**Change:** Refactor\n<!-- change_assessment_end -->\n\n### Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n  participant certify_joint_acyclic\n  participant JointGraph\n  participant MoveIndex\n  participant acyclic\n  certify_joint_acyclic->>JointGraph: Build precomputed graph data\n  JointGraph->>MoveIndex: Propagate copied-variable flows\n  MoveIndex-->>JointGraph: Return reachable positions\n  JointGraph-->>certify_joint_acyclic: Provide moves, frontiers, and ownership\n  certify_joint_acyclic->>acyclic: Check dependency graph for cycles\n  acyclic-->>certify_joint_acyclic: Return cycle result\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- final_review_risk_start -->\n**Merge Risk:** _⚪ Minimal_ · up to `92068`\n<!-- final_review_risk_coverage:{\"sourceCommitId\":\"92068d6292b81aefe620564ffbbfbb59061b78b1\",\"coveredCommitId\":\"92068d6292b81aefe620564ffbbfbb59061b78b1\",\"kind\":\"reviewed\"} -->\n\nThis change speeds up joint-acyclicity computation while keeping the same verdicts, and no concrete problems were identified. It appears ready to merge after normal checks.\n<!-- final_review_risk_end -->\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_override_start -->\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> ## Pre-merge checks failed\n> \n> Please resolve all errors before merging. Addressing warnings is optional.\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_override_end -->\n\n### ❌ Failed checks (1 error)\n\n|     Check name     | Status  | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                | Resolution                                                                         |\n| :----------------: | :------ | :----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :--------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Docstring Coverage | ❌ Error | Docstring coverage is 71.43% which is insufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%. Docstring coverage is scoped to functions touched by this diff. Analyzed 7 functions across 1 files. | Write docstrings for the functions missing them to satisfy the coverage 