/summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 22193fc44ce4255e648d388786ef5c3ed905170d and 1d5d7f36dd84ba90a3ae762ea5dcf9ff825654ad.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⛔ Files ignored due to path filters: 2</summary>\n\n* `Cargo.lock` is excluded by `!**/*.lock`\n* `fuzz/Cargo.lock` is excluded by `!**/*.lock`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing: 6</summary>\n\n* `crates/logic/Cargo.toml`\n* `crates/logic/src/physical/chase.rs`\n* `crates/logic/src/physical/chase.tests.rs`\n* `crates/logic/src/physical/seminaive/property/datatype.tests.rs`\n* `crates/logic/src/reason/artifacts.tests.rs`\n* `crates/logic/src/reason/value.rs`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔗 Linked repositories identified</summary>\n\nCodeRabbit considers these linked repositories for cross-repo context during reviews:\n\n- [`Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf`](https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf) _(auto-detected)_\n- [`Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-gts`](https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-gts) _(auto-detected)_\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>💤 Files with no reviewable changes: 1</summary>\n\n* crates/logic/Cargo.toml\n\n</details>\n\n**Included review availability:** This review used your included allowance. 3 included reviews remain after this review. Your included PR review attempts over the past 7 days set your current allowance at 5 reviews per hour.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Additional context used</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📚 Code guidelines: 1</summary>\n\n```\n.github/copilot-instructions.md — auto-discovered\n```\n\n</details><details>\n<summary>📓 Path-based instructions: 2</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Ensure Rust code is formatted with `cargo fmt` and passes `cargo clippy` with warnings treated as errors.</summary>\n\n\n**📄 CodeRabbit inference engine (.github/copilot-instructions.md)**\n\n**Files:**\n- `crates/logic/src/reason/value.rs`\n- `crates/logic/src/physical/seminaive/property/datatype.tests.rs`\n- `crates/logic/src/physical/chase.tests.rs`\n- `crates/logic/src/reason/artifacts.tests.rs`\n- `crates/logic/src/physical/chase.rs`\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Refer to the project-root `AGENTS.md` for available `make` targets and developer commands, such as `make check` and `gmeow-dev sync`.</summary>\n\n\n**📄 CodeRabbit inference engine (.github/copilot-instructions.md)**\n\n**Files:**\n- `crates/logic/src/reason/value.rs`\n- `crates/logic/src/physical/seminaive/property/datatype.tests.rs`\n- `crates/logic/src/physical/chase.tests.rs`\n- `crates/logic/src/reason/artifacts.tests.rs`\n- `crates/logic/src/physical/chase.rs`\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details>\n<summary>🔀 Multi-repo context Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf, Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-gts</summary>\n\n## Linked repositories findings\n\n### `Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf`\n\n- PurRDF’s OWL parser accepts qualified cardinality fillers via `owl:onDataRange` and routes them through the same expression path as `owl:onClass` (`crates/entail/src/owl_dl/parser.rs:988-1000`). The PR’s ontology changes from `logic:onClass logic:Thing` to `logic:onDataRange rdfs:Literal` are compatible with this parser contract. [::Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf::]\n- PurRDF’s datatype-range engine explicitly places `xsd:anyURI` in its unmodeled remainder, producing undecided results rather than native range proofs (`crates/xsd/src/range.rs` module documentation). Any new ontology-side `anyURI` reasoning must therefore remain implemented in the consuming reasoner rather than relying on PurRDF range entailment. [::Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf::]\n\n### `Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-gts`\n\n- GTS compares literals by exact lexical form, datatype IRI, language, and direction; it does not apply datatype lexical canonicalization (`docs/GTS-SPEC.md:700-706`). The PR’s `anyURI` whitespace/facet semantics must not be expected to arise from GTS transport. [::Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-gts::]\n- Rust and Go GTS validators accept `xsd:anyURI` lexical forms unchanged (`rust/src/xsd.rs:114`, `go/xsd/xsd.go:106`), confirming that URI facet interpretation belongs to the reasoning layer.\n- Untyped literals are defaulted to `xsd:string` during GTS interning (`rust/src/rdf.rs:985-1002`), so removing language tags from the PR’s constraint-message literals does not alter their datatype during transport. [::Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-gts::]\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔇 Additional comments: 9</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>crates/logic/src/reason/artifacts.tests.rs: 1</summary><blockquote>\n\n`6-9`: LGTM!\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 33-38, 40-96, 98-142, 144-162, 174-179, 211-276, 302-329, 373-378, 408-413, 428-440, 455-455, 507-507, 551-551, 574-579, 598-612, 626-626, 648-652, 670-670, 681-683\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:7928de3e7ab50dba20f51bd1 -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>crates/logic/src/physical/seminaive/property/datatype.tests.rs: 1</summary><blockquote>\n\n`164-202`: LGTM!\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:b1cb176eb090179d055b2c7b -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>crates/logic/src/reason/value.rs: 1</summary><blockquote>\n\n`24-26`: LGTM!\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 225-247\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:921e2c53b98a899aed286a90 -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>crates/logic/src/physical/chase.rs: 5</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1381-1381`: LGTM!\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:904da55530288bc3f7e6f319 -->\n\n---\n\n`1564-1573`: LGTM!\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 1606-1609, 1630-1691, 1716-1716, 1735-1756, 1764-1764, 1784-1784\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:d184aa5f0eb63e44048e90bb -->\n\n---\n\n`1848-1862`: LGTM!\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 1869-1869, 1873-1873, 1897-1897\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:9ef18a44b3eb632c5b6107d7 -->\n\n---\n\n`2052-2052`: LGTM!\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 2057-2057, 2063-2063, 2086-2086, 2109-2125, 2152-2153\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:595be2954e2d95cea3149d2e -->\n\n---\n\n`3578-3578`: LGTM!\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 3590-3593, 3627-3627, 3736-3746, 