.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1802-current-comments.md:132:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1802-current-comments.md:133:## Linked repositories findings
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1802-current-comments.md:134:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1802-current-comments.md:135:### `Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf`
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1802-current-comments.md:136:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1802-current-comments.md:137:- Qualified cardinality restrictions support both `owl:onClass` and `owl:onDataRange` through the same filler-resolution path, so the PR’s ontology changes to `logic:onDataRange rdfs:Literal` are compatible with PurRDF’s parser contract. `crates/entail/src/owl_dl/parser.rs:989-1000` [::Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf::]
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1802-current-comments.md:138:- PurRDF treats `xsd:anyURI` as a data-range name syntactically, but its range engine leaves `xsd:anyURI` in the unmodeled remainder; `rdfs:Literal` represents the whole data domain. The PR’s specialized `anyURI` reasoning therefore remains responsibility of GMEOW’s native reasoner. `crates/entail/src/owl_dl/parser.rs:606-618`, `crates/xsd/src/range.rs:44-49,167-170` [::Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf::]
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1802-current-comments.md:139:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1802-current-comments.md:140:### `Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-gts`
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1802-current-comments.md:141:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1802-current-comments.md:142:- GTS is explicitly ontology-independent and treats GMEOW semantics as a downstream profile concern. The PR’s chase/admission changes do not require a GTS core change. `docs/GTS-SPEC.md:43-47` [::Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-gts::]
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1802-current-comments.md:143:- GTS compares literals by exact lexical form, datatype, language tag, and direction without datatype canonicalization. Its XSD helper accepts `xsd:anyURI` lexical forms unchanged. Thus the PR’s XML-whitespace normalization and `anyURI` equality/facet behavior must remain in the reasoning layer rather than being delegated to GTS transport. `docs/GTS-SPEC.md:700-706`, `go/xsd/xsd.go:1-8,95-105` [::Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-gts::]
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1802-current-comments.md:144:
