.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1802-current-comments.md:472:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1802-current-comments.md:473:The native-rule migration has passed its expanded development controls: 951 of 952 cases passed in the expanded run, and the sole fixture-identity assertion was corrected to match its authored plain literal and passed its focused recheck. This covers the native RDF rule round trip, all CL dialect metadata round trips, all six atom-scope dimensions, gate controls, the reviewed `!sameTerm` golden, and the production-profile GTS carrier-root/write/import/read control. The latter preserves a dynamic predicate, directional literal, negation, guard and rule scope through the actual statement layer. Principles 2, 3, 4, 7, 17 and 18 apply.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1802-current-comments.md:474:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1802-current-comments.md:475:The first combined full gate failed helper hygiene: 716 default-hasher copies against 705 and 27 collection copies against 19. Those findings remain part of the failed run. The uncommitted repair uses PurRDF's fixed hasher in the affected native tables and its existing collection builders/walker in eight counted copies, plus the IR projection walker. Cell identities, native value kinds, graph scopes and malformed-list errors are retained. The collection count returns to 19; the hasher count falls to 704. The complete generated debt diff was inspected: its only change lowers the hasher count from 705 to 704. No ceiling or duplicate group was raised.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1802-current-comments.md:476:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1802-current-comments.md:477:The compiler directly names the already-linked `purrdf-core` workspace package to call these collection APIs; both locks add only that edge, without package/version/profile/feature changes. A new product regression requires malformed selected value lists to fail shape admission rather than produce a weaker shape. The latest lint passes. The affected expanded tests and helper gate are still running, so these additional repairs are not yet reported as validated.
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1802-current-comments.md:478:
.stage/perf-logic-finish-merged-pipeline/raw/pr1802-current-comments.md:479:The optimized producer and first full run remain in flight. The coordinator rechecks source/configuration after compilation and refuses a receipt when they changed, so the earlier build cannot qualify these later edits. A fresh required full qualification is still needed after the repairs settle; it is an explicitly required retry of a failed gate. No test constructs the ontology corpus, no corpus-backed test has been waived, and no canonical commit, fresh-source CI pass, completion audit, readiness or merge is claimed. The published PR head remains `b797a315e`.
