ogic/src/physical/seminaive/joint/input/tests.rs`\n- `crates/logic/src/physical/effects/value_flow.rs`\n- `crates/logic/src/physical/chase.tests.rs`\n- `crates/logic/src/reason/value.rs`\n- `crates/logic/src/physical/seminaive/property/datatype.tests.rs`\n- `crates/logic/src/physical/seminaive/joint.rs`\n- `slices/grounding/lang/module.ttl`\n- `slices/grounding/math/module.ttl`\n- `crates/logic/src/physical/seminaive/joint/input/admission.rs`\n- `slices/grounding/logic/module.ttl`\n- `crates/logic/src/physical/chase.rs`\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details>\n<summary>\ud83d\udd00 Multi-repo context Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf, Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-gts</summary>\n\n## Linked repositories findings\n\n### `Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf`\n\n- The OWL parser recognizes `xsd:anyURI` as a data range and resolves qualified cardinality through `owl:onDataRange` (`crates/entail/src/owl_dl/parser.rs:604-611, 988-1000`). This matches the PR\u2019s migration from `logic:onClass logic:Thing` to `logic:onDataRange rdfs:Literal`. [::Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf::]\n- PurRDF\u2019s native `XsdDatatype` enum excludes `anyURI`; `parse_by_iri` therefore treats it as an opaque/unmodeled datatype (`crates/xsd/src/datatype.rs:145-234`, `crates/xsd/src/value.rs:373-376`). Its range engine explicitly places `xsd:anyURI` in the undecided remainder (`crates/xsd/src/range.rs:40-48`). Any ontology behavior requiring native `anyURI` membership or facet reasoning may therefore remain undecided when delegated to PurRDF. [::Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf::]\n\n### `Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-gts`\n\n- GTS preserves explicit literal datatypes and defaults only literals without language/direction/datatype to `xsd:string` (`docs/GTS-SPEC.md \u00a77.1`). The PR\u2019s plain `logic:message` literals and explicit datatype-property restrictions are compatible with this transport contract. [::Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-gts::]\n- The Rust and Go GTS validators accept `xsd:anyURI` lexical forms unchanged rather than applying URI-specific normalization (`rust/src/xsd.rs:114`, `go/xsd/xsd.go:106`). Any `anyURI` facet semantics must therefore be established by the ontology/reasoning layer before or after GTS transport, not by GTS itself. [::Blackcat-Informatics/gmeow-gts::]\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>\ud83d\udd07 Additional comments: 19</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>crates/logic/src/physical/effects/value_flow.rs: 1</summary><blockquote>\n\n`3259-3264`: LGTM!\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:f4db3ea5c4a2f7513dc46901 -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>crates/logic/src/physical/seminaive/property/datatype.tests.rs: 1</summary><blockquote>\n\n`164-223`: LGTM!\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:5dbe75177f458e3c232ce222 -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>slices/core/affect/module.ttl: 1</summary><blockquote>\n\n`3192-3192`: LGTM!\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:3b8357945a0a5c6d5ca99d3e -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>slices/core/agentic/module.ttl: 1</summary><blockquote>\n\n`151-152`: LGTM!\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:b9be84945b4d0f756919a810 -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>slices/core/calendar/module.ttl: 1</summary><blockquote>\n\n`832-833`: LGTM!\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:ae39586a4a174351fbfdad23 -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>slices/core/gts/module.ttl: 1</summary><blockquote>\n\n`3214-3215`: LGTM!\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:4dd796eba075a097f16b9e54 -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>slices/core/norms/module.ttl: 1</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1233-1233`: LGTM!\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 1368-1368\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:6dc7e84c4ab621b0c6333103 -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>slices/grounding/lang/module.ttl: 1</summary><blockquote>\n\n`10990-10990`: **\ud83d\uddc4\ufe0f Data Integrity & Integration**\n\nThe concern is refuted. `derive_validation_shapes` lowers `logic:onDataRange` qualified maxima to a plain `sh:maxCount` with the same bound. Both restrictions